1
00:00:07,889 --> 00:00:13,263
The Life of Muhammadﷺ, The Madinan Period, Volume 1

2
00:00:13,390 --> 00:00:15,652
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki,

3
00:00:18,970 --> 00:00:21,589
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

4
00:00:21,646 --> 00:00:27,878
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْراَّ

5
00:00:28,335 --> 00:00:32,750
Rasool Allah ﷺ sends Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة) and Zaid Bin Harissa (زيد بن حارثه)

6
00:00:33,206 --> 00:00:35,402
to deliver the news to the people of Madina.

7
00:00:35,666 --> 00:00:40,151
Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة) goes to Awali(عوالي), the upper areas of Madina

8
00:00:40,194 --> 00:00:44,297
 and he delivers the news to each house of Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار),

9
00:00:44,660 --> 00:00:48,603
 while Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه) goes to the center of Madina to deliver the news.

10
00:00:48,643 --> 00:00:53,299
Now Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه) was riding on the camel of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

11
00:00:54,015 --> 00:00:57,454
So, when he came in, delivering the news and saying that

12
00:00:57,501 --> 00:00:58,777
 Ut'bah Bin Rabiyah(عتبة بن ربيعة) was killed,

13
00:00:58,817 --> 00:01:00,094
Shaibah Bin Rabiyah(شيبة بن ربيعة) was killed

14
00:01:00,144 --> 00:01:01,779
Ibn Al-Hajjaj(إبن الحجاج) were killed,

15
00:01:02,071 --> 00:01:03,434
Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) was killed

16
00:01:03,474 --> 00:01:07,522
and he was mentioning the famous names of the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), who were killed.

17
00:01:07,912 --> 00:01:10,021
The Munafiqeen(منافقين) and the Yahood(يهود) said;

18
00:01:10,523 --> 00:01:13,521
This man doesn't know what he's talking about, he's confused

19
00:01:13,934 --> 00:01:16,021
and he has run away from the battlefield,

20
00:01:16,418 --> 00:01:18,643
and Muhammad(محمد) himself was killed

21
00:01:18,901 --> 00:01:21,675
and the evidence is that Zaid(زيد) is riding his camel.

22
00:01:22,535 --> 00:01:24,894
And they went around spreading this news.

23
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:27,347
So, Usamah(اسامه) said: I went to my father's Zaid(زيد)

24
00:01:27,397 --> 00:01:31,604
because Usamah(اسامه) was left behind, he stayed in Madina to care for Ruqayyah(رقية).

25
00:01:31,830 --> 00:01:35,733
Usamah(اسامه) and Uthman(عثمان) stayed behind to care for Ruqayyah(رقية) the daughter of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

26
00:01:35,765 --> 00:01:36,498
 So, Usamah(اسامه) said;

27
00:01:36,757 --> 00:01:40,813
I went to my father and said; O, Father is the news that you're delivering, true.?

28
00:01:40,973 --> 00:01:42,846
He said, Yes, my son it is true.

29
00:01:43,021 --> 00:01:46,253
People were going to Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة) and saying is that news true?

30
00:01:46,628 --> 00:01:48,162
He would say; yes, the news is true

31
00:01:48,202 --> 00:01:50,618
 and tomorrow Rasool Allah ﷺ is going to bring the captives.

32
00:01:50,985 --> 00:01:53,930
It was so difficult for people to believe what happened,

33
00:01:54,263 --> 00:01:57,422
a force of little over 300 defeats a 1000

34
00:01:57,670 --> 00:02:01,840
and then kills the most famous names of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), all of them are dead

35
00:02:02,556 --> 00:02:05,018
Ut'bah(عتبة), Shaibah(شيبة), Al-Waleed(الوليد), Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل),

36
00:02:05,482 --> 00:02:07,769
Nabeeha Al-Munabbah(نبيحه ألمنبه), Ibn Al-Hajjaj(إبن ألحجاج) and others,

37
00:02:07,809 --> 00:02:09,504
 all of them were killed on that day.

38
00:02:09,732 --> 00:02:15,336
And then other leaders, such as Sohail Ibn Amr(سهيل إبن عمرو), are captured, taken as prisoners.

39
00:02:15,752 --> 00:02:17,749
So, it was too good to be true,

40
00:02:18,683 --> 00:02:27,328
but the next day, Rasool Allah ﷺ does come in with the prisoners and the victory of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

41
00:02:27,662 --> 00:02:31,781
Now, the prisoners were placed in a certain location

42
00:02:32,103 --> 00:02:35,500
and Sodah(سؤده), the wife of Rasool Allah ﷺ

43
00:02:36,024 --> 00:02:41,533
when she saw Sohail Bin Amr(سهيل إبن عمرو) with his hands tied to his neck.

44
00:02:42,424 --> 00:02:44,469
And this was one of the noblemen of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

45
00:02:45,214 --> 00:02:48,746
She said: Why didn't you die as nobleman?

46
00:02:49,337 --> 00:02:53,498
Why did you allow yourselves to be humiliated and to be in this state?

47
00:02:53,578 --> 00:02:55,104
Why didn't you, die as nobleman.

48
00:02:55,144 --> 00:02:56,465
 اَفَلَا اَمِتُّمْ كِرَامًا

49
00:02:56,848 --> 00:03:00,224
Rasool Allah ﷺ overlooked that statement and said;

50
00:03:00,551 --> 00:03:02,658
اَعَلَی لَّلّهُ وَرَسُوْلِهِ تُحَّرِّضِيِنْ

51
00:03:03,291 --> 00:03:06,205
Are you asking them to fight Allah and His Messenger?

52
00:03:06,843 --> 00:03:08,990
Because in fact, what she was saying is,

53
00:03:09,339 --> 00:03:14,113
why didn't you fight rather than be held captive, the way you are,

54
00:03:14,470 --> 00:03:18,551
 and when she is saying why didn't he fight, who would he fight against.?

55
00:03:18,646 --> 00:03:20,661
He would be fighting against Rasool Allah ﷺ.

56
00:03:20,957 --> 00:03:23,742
So, Sodah(سؤده) said: She apologized, to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said,

57
00:03:23,976 --> 00:03:26,211
O Messenger of Allah, When I saw him in that state,

58
00:03:26,583 --> 00:03:28,790
I couldn't, but say such a statement.

59
00:03:29,546 --> 00:03:33,435
Her emotions overwhelmed her, when she saw Sohail(سهيل) in that state.

60
00:03:33,546 --> 00:03:39,227
 So, it tells you that the leaders of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were humiliated because of their disbelief and Kuffr(كفر)

61
00:03:39,359 --> 00:03:42,946
and the way they dealt with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,

62
00:03:43,219 --> 00:03:44,307
most of them were killed

63
00:03:44,367 --> 00:03:47,926
 and then you have the people like SohailIbn Amr(سهيل إبن عمرو) are tied in ropes.

64
00:03:49,294 --> 00:03:56,992
Rasool Allah ﷺ stopped at Ar-Rohaa(ألروحاء) to receive congratulations, from all of the people that were coming to visit him.

65
00:03:57,527 --> 00:04:00,665
And when the people were coming to congratulate him

66
00:04:00,887 --> 00:04:02,046
one of the Ansaar(ألأنصار) said:

67
00:04:02,086 --> 00:04:04,268
What are you congratulating us for,

68
00:04:04,582 --> 00:04:10,979
We have only met old, bald men, like camels awaiting slaughter

69
00:04:11,231 --> 00:04:12,408
and we slaughtered them.

70
00:04:12,638 --> 00:04:17,655
 Rasool Allah ﷺ said, Hey my cousin, Don't say that, these are the chiefs.

71
00:04:19,097 --> 00:04:21,192
This Ansaari(اَنصاري) was saying it was so easy,

72
00:04:21,735 --> 00:04:26,168
those people whom we faced are old men who don't know how to fight.

73
00:04:27,126 --> 00:04:32,882
It was Allah who helped you, through the angels, otherwise we couldn't have defeated such an army.

74
00:04:32,951 --> 00:04:35,737
 So, these are strong men, it was a strong opponent,

75
00:04:36,135 --> 00:04:38,490
but Allahعَزّوجَلّ assisted us, and helped us.

76
00:04:39,781 --> 00:04:44,923
The news was delivered to Makkah by a man called Al-Haithamaan Al-Khuza'ee(ألحُيْسمان ألخزاعي)

77
00:04:45,519 --> 00:04:48,858
Al-Haithamaan Al-Khuza'ee(ألحُيْسمان ألخزاعي) rushes into Makkah and says,

78
00:04:49,092 --> 00:04:50,308
Abul Hakam(ابو الكحم) was killed,

79
00:04:50,461 --> 00:04:51,469
Ut'ba(عتبة) was killed,

80
00:04:51,525 --> 00:04:52,509
Shaibah(شيبة) was killed,

81
00:04:52,564 --> 00:04:53,468
Al-Waleed(الوليد) was killed,

82
00:04:53,508 --> 00:04:54,820
and he's going down the list,

83
00:04:55,375 --> 00:04:56,852
and Ummayyah(اميه) was killed.

84
00:04:57,144 --> 00:05:00,521
Safwaan Ibn Ummayyah(صفوان ابن اميه) was listening.

85
00:05:00,996 --> 00:05:03,521
And he said: This man has lost his mind.

86
00:05:04,261 --> 00:05:09,052
Ask him about me, to make sure that, he isn't crazy.

87
00:05:09,431 --> 00:05:10,339
So, they asked him.

88
00:05:10,521 --> 00:05:12,196
What about Safwaan(صفوان), what happened to him.?

89
00:05:12,236 --> 00:05:14,252
He said; Safwaan(صفوان) is sitting right there.

90
00:05:14,510 --> 00:05:18,397
And I have seen the death of his father and his brother with my own eyes.

91
00:05:19,496 --> 00:05:23,373
And for the people of Makkah it was too bad to be true.

92
00:05:23,539 --> 00:05:29,451
 How could Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) be killed, and Ummayyah(اميه) be killed, and Ut'ba(عتبة) be killed?

93
00:05:29,491 --> 00:05:30,435
 It's impossible,

94
00:05:30,849 --> 00:05:33,168
but surely the news was sinking in.

95
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:37,055
Abu Lahab(ابولهب) was one of those, who stayed behind,

96
00:05:37,505 --> 00:05:39,739
but he sent somebody in his place to fight.

97
00:05:40,881 --> 00:05:45,333
Raafiah(رافع) says that I was a servant of Al-Abbas(العباس)

98
00:05:45,851 --> 00:05:50,402
and our household was Muslim, Me and Al-Abbas(العباس) and Ummul Fazal(أم الفضل),

99
00:05:50,442 --> 00:05:53,288
 Ummul Fazal(أم الفضل) is the wife ofAl-Abbas(العباس), we were Muslim.

100
00:05:53,795 --> 00:05:56,316
And I used to make arrows.

101
00:05:56,968 --> 00:06:01,620
So, I was sitting in the pavilion around the Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه), sharpening arrows,

102
00:06:02,001 --> 00:06:05,156
while Abu Lahab(ابولهب) was sitting with his back towards me,

103
00:06:05,693 --> 00:06:09,059
when one of the fighters from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) approached.

104
00:06:09,585 --> 00:06:12,801
So, Abu Lahab(ابولهب) said; Come and tell us the news of what happened?

105
00:06:13,787 --> 00:06:16,258
So, the man came and he said;

106
00:06:16,828 --> 00:06:18,595
As soon as the fighting started

107
00:06:18,991 --> 00:06:23,192
we handed them over ourselves to be killed and to be taken as captives.

108
00:06:24,265 --> 00:06:26,904
But I don't blame them for it,

109
00:06:27,388 --> 00:06:30,583
because we were facing men in white clothes

110
00:06:31,221 --> 00:06:35,875
on horses, between the heavens and earth, and nothing can stop them.

111
00:06:36,696 --> 00:06:42,353
So, he was saying that it is true that we were defeated by the army of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

112
00:06:42,394 --> 00:06:44,377
 But we don't give credit to them.

113
00:06:44,417 --> 00:06:50,777
It was some other people wearing white who defeated us and nothing could stop that force.

114
00:06:51,615 --> 00:06:55,634
When Raafiah(رافع) heard that, he said, In the name of Allah, those are the angels.

115
00:06:56,857 --> 00:07:02,348
Abu Lahab(ابولهب) turned around and punched him in the face, such a blow.

116
00:07:03,529 --> 00:07:06,026
Raafiah(رافع) said: So, I started fighting back

117
00:07:06,073 --> 00:07:09,022
but Abu Lahab(ابولهب) was stronger than me and I was a weak man

118
00:07:09,410 --> 00:07:12,219
So, he was sitting over me and beating me hard,

119
00:07:12,568 --> 00:07:17,932
when Ummul Fazal(أم الفضل) came with a rod and she hit Abu Lahab(ابولهب) on the head

120
00:07:18,312 --> 00:07:23,469
and told him; You are taking advantage that his master is not around.

121
00:07:23,802 --> 00:07:25,222
 Then Abu Lahab(ابولهب) left.

122
00:07:27,051 --> 00:07:32,837
Raafiah(رافع) says, that Abu Lahab(ابولهب) was afflicted by disease after that and died a week later.

123
00:07:33,763 --> 00:07:38,162
And he said this particular disease would terrify the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

124
00:07:38,270 --> 00:07:41,593
And if somebody is inflicted with that disease, they wouldn't want to go next to him.

125
00:07:42,322 --> 00:07:47,471
So, Abu Lahab(ابولهب) died and remained in his house for three days until, his body was decomposing,

126
00:07:48,062 --> 00:07:49,611
and nobody wants to bury him.

127
00:07:50,112 --> 00:07:52,581
So, The people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) went to his two sons and said,

128
00:07:52,947 --> 00:07:57,345
I mean, shame on you, your father, his body is decomposing, and you don't want to bury him.

129
00:07:57,385 --> 00:07:59,298
 They said, well, we're afraid of that disease.

130
00:08:00,455 --> 00:08:02,865
So what they did is,

131
00:08:02,924 --> 00:08:06,442
they ended up dragging him and placing him next to a wall.

132
00:08:06,482 --> 00:08:09,636
They didn't even dig a grave for him, they placed him next to wall,

133
00:08:09,785 --> 00:08:12,298
and then they threw stones over him to cover his body.

134
00:08:12,474 --> 00:08:15,756
That is the humiliation that he suffered, even in his death.

135
00:08:17,803 --> 00:08:23,676
The people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) in order not to have the Muslims rejoice at their misfortune

136
00:08:24,266 --> 00:08:29,870
prevented anyone from crying publicly for the dead.

137
00:08:30,489 --> 00:08:33,663
 So, there was no wailing allowed.

138
00:08:33,965 --> 00:08:41,664
Also, they refused to allow anybody to investigate the issue of ransoming, the prisoners.

139
00:08:42,379 --> 00:08:46,885
So that Muhammadﷺ will not raise the price of ransom.

140
00:08:48,289 --> 00:08:51,098
Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر), He says about this.

141
00:08:52,153 --> 00:08:58,862
He said, I observe that Allah's forcing them to forego mourning for their dead

142
00:08:59,340 --> 00:09:06,174
was part of the totality of His punishment, of those of them that remained alive at that time,

143
00:09:06,782 --> 00:09:11,411
for weeping for the dead contributes to the recovery of the grieving heart.

144
00:09:12,296 --> 00:09:19,600
So, this prevention of mourning was in fact more of a torment for the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

145
00:09:19,751 --> 00:09:20,917
 the ones who are living.

146
00:09:21,755 --> 00:09:23,330
And then he says, Ibn Is'haqq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ) stated

147
00:09:23,370 --> 00:09:27,458
Al-Aswad Ibn Al-Muttalib(ألأسود ابن المطلب) was afflicted with the loss of three of his sons.

148
00:09:27,892 --> 00:09:32,878
This was an old man, he was already blind, and he lost three of his sons

149
00:09:33,537 --> 00:09:37,684
and he wasn't allowed to mourn their deaths.

150
00:09:38,307 --> 00:09:42,531
So, one night he hears a woman weeping.

151
00:09:43,229 --> 00:09:47,018
 So, he said; Go and see if mourning has become permissible

152
00:09:47,731 --> 00:09:50,005
are Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) now be wailing their dead,

153
00:09:50,432 --> 00:09:56,631
perhaps I will now be able to lament the loss of Abu Hakima(ابوحكيمه), his eldest son,

154
00:09:57,196 --> 00:09:58,656
for I am in great pain.

155
00:09:59,818 --> 00:10:02,738
So, they went to find out why the woman was crying?

156
00:10:02,789 --> 00:10:05,129
They found out she's crying because he lost a camel.

157
00:10:05,633 --> 00:10:07,811
So, he says these lines of poetry, he said,

158
00:10:08,179 --> 00:10:14,052
Is she weeping because of a camel of hers has gone astray...

159
00:10:14,421 --> 00:10:17,383
And so insomnia keeps her from sleeping...

160
00:10:17,806 --> 00:10:19,827
Do not weep over young camel...

161
00:10:20,176 --> 00:10:22,848
But over Badr(بدر) that ruined all hopes...

162
00:10:23,447 --> 00:10:27,507
over Badr(بدر) and the elite of the Bannu Husais(بنو هصيص) and Makhzoom(مخذوم)...

163
00:10:27,786 --> 00:10:29,710
And the tribe of Abul Waleed(أبو الوليد)...

164
00:10:30,133 --> 00:10:31,903
And weep if you weep at all...

165
00:10:32,233 --> 00:10:34,437
For Abu Aqeel(أبو عقيل)... And for Harris(حارث)...

166
00:10:34,678 --> 00:10:39,226
The Lion of lions, Weep for them all and do not hold back...

167
00:10:39,713 --> 00:10:43,140
For there is none, The like of Abu Hakeema(ابوحكيمة)...

168
00:10:43,520 --> 00:10:47,971
after them it is other men who rule, and had it not been for Badr(بدر)...

169
00:10:48,294 --> 00:10:50,047
They would not have come to lead...

170
00:10:51,079 --> 00:10:56,401
So, this poor old man wasn't even allowed to mourn the loss of his three sons.

171
00:10:56,472 --> 00:10:57,131
Why?

172
00:10:57,273 --> 00:11:03,639
So, that the news wouldn't reach to Muhammadﷺ that the Kuffar(كفار) of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) are suffering

173
00:11:03,696 --> 00:11:06,178
because of their dead, they wanted to show they don't care about it.

174
00:11:06,397 --> 00:11:10,869
And they wanted to show that, they don't care about the ransom of the captives.

175
00:11:12,282 --> 00:11:16,897
 Surat-Al-Anfaal(سورة الأنفال) was revealed, after the Ghazwa(غزوة) of Badr(بدر).

176
00:11:17,383 --> 00:11:22,854
Ubadah Bin Samit(عبادة بن الصامت) says about the first verses of Surat-Al-Anfaal(سورة الأنفال).

177
00:11:23,499 --> 00:11:27,348
They were revealed about us, The Muslims at Badr(بدر).

178
00:11:28,007 --> 00:11:30,414
When we disputed the issue of booty

179
00:11:31,236 --> 00:11:32,728
وَسَاعَتْ فِيْ اَخْلَاقُنَا

180
00:11:32,768 --> 00:11:35,680
and we were disputing with one another about it.

181
00:11:36,306 --> 00:11:41,745
What happened was the Muslims were three groups one group was protecting Rasool Allah ﷺ,

182
00:11:42,170 --> 00:11:44,627
the second group was pursuing the enemy

183
00:11:44,952 --> 00:11:47,773
and the third group were collecting the spoils of war.

184
00:11:48,549 --> 00:11:51,682
So, the ones who collected the spoils of war said, these belong to us.

185
00:11:52,517 --> 00:11:54,393
The ones, who protected Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

186
00:11:54,433 --> 00:11:57,103
 No, we want our share because we are protecting Rasool Ullah.

187
00:11:57,680 --> 00:11:59,389
And the ones who are pursuing the enemy said;

188
00:11:59,429 --> 00:12:03,381
If it wasn't for us you wouldn't have any spoils of war.

189
00:12:04,508 --> 00:12:07,876
So, they disputed and they were arguing

190
00:12:08,360 --> 00:12:13,287
and Allahعَزّوجَلّ revealed the Ayaat(آيات) of Surat-Al-Anfaal(سورة الأنفال).

191
00:12:13,319 --> 00:12:16,630
يَسْأَلُونَكَ عَنِ الْأَنْفَالِ ۖ قُلِ الْأَنْفَالُ لِلَّهِ وَالرَّسُولِ ۖ

192
00:12:18,013 --> 00:12:23,233
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says: They ask you, O Muhammad(محمد) about the bounties of war,

193
00:12:23,273 --> 00:12:28,906
say the decision concerning bounties is for Allah and the Messenger.

194
00:12:29,099 --> 00:12:34,160
Therefore all of the boundaries of war were taken from them, and given to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

195
00:12:34,289 --> 00:12:38,955
 It belongs to Allah and Rasool Ullah, all of it was taken away.

196
00:12:39,733 --> 00:12:41,691
 And then Allah says; So, fear Allah

197
00:12:42,084 --> 00:12:48,141
and amend that which is between you and obey Allah and His Messenger, if you should be believers.

198
00:12:48,481 --> 00:12:52,477
So, this Ayaah(آية) is teaching the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) that they should have Taqwa(تقوى),

199
00:12:53,138 --> 00:12:55,558
you cannot fight Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) without Taqwa(تقوى).

200
00:12:55,879 --> 00:13:00,991
Number two, and amend that which is between you and you have to have unity

201
00:13:01,299 --> 00:13:04,801
for fighters Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله), they have to be one.

202
00:13:05,381 --> 00:13:08,962
And number three and obey Allah and His Messenger,

203
00:13:09,410 --> 00:13:10,845
you have to have discipline

204
00:13:11,381 --> 00:13:13,666
fighters without discipline are not going to succeed.

205
00:13:14,058 --> 00:13:18,097
So, they have to have discipline and obedience of the leader.

206
00:13:18,394 --> 00:13:23,600
So, these are three essential qualities for Al-Mujahideen(المجاهدين) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله),

207
00:13:23,680 --> 00:13:29,476
 Taqwa(تقوى) and unity, and discipline and obedience of the leader.

208
00:13:30,773 --> 00:13:37,817
And then Allahعَزّوجَلّ gives the ruling regarding, how the spoils of war are divided?

209
00:13:38,455 --> 00:13:39,742
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

210
00:13:40,019 --> 00:13:50,392
وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّمَا غَنِمْتُمْ مِنْ شَيْءٍ فَأَنَّ لِلَّهِ خُمُسَهُ وَلِلرَّسُولِ

211
00:13:50,865 --> 00:13:58,359
وَلِلرَّسُولِ وَلِذِي الْقُرْبَىٰ وَالْيَتَامَىٰ وَالْمَسَاكِينِ وَابْنِ السَّبِيلِ

212
00:13:58,706 --> 00:14:09,825
إِنْ كُنْتُمْ آمَنْتُمْ بِاللَّهِ وَمَا أَنْزَلْنَا عَلَىٰ عَبْدِنَا يَوْمَ الْفُرْقَانِ

213
00:14:10,210 --> 00:14:15,140
يَوْمَ الْفُرْقَانِ يَوْمَ الْتَقَى الْجَمْعَانِ ۗ

214
00:14:15,322 --> 00:14:20,103
وَاللَّهُ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ۝

215
00:14:20,475 --> 00:14:23,965
And know that anything you obtain of war booty.

216
00:14:24,557 --> 00:14:29,942
Indeed, for Allah is one fifth of it and for the messenger

217
00:14:30,256 --> 00:14:34,131
and for his nearer relatives, and the orphans, the needy

218
00:14:34,521 --> 00:14:36,136
and the stranded traveler.

219
00:14:36,484 --> 00:14:43,245
If you have believed in Allah and in that which we sent down to our servant, on the day of criterion,

220
00:14:43,443 --> 00:14:45,383
 The day when the two armies met

221
00:14:45,739 --> 00:14:48,749
and Allah over all things is competent.

222
00:14:49,712 --> 00:14:53,352
So, the ruling regarding the spoils of war is as follows,

223
00:14:53,923 --> 00:14:58,666
They are divided into five portions, five equal portions

224
00:14:59,509 --> 00:15:03,687
four of those, five portions are distributed among the fighters.

225
00:15:04,083 --> 00:15:07,540
So, 80% if we convert it to percentage,

226
00:15:07,826 --> 00:15:13,016
80% of the spoils of war are split among the fighters.

227
00:15:14,165 --> 00:15:17,153
The foot soldier receives one share

228
00:15:17,573 --> 00:15:23,996
and the horsemen receive three shares, the cavalry three shares each.

229
00:15:25,323 --> 00:15:30,414
The remaining 20% is then divided into five portions,

230
00:15:30,454 --> 00:15:32,557
 so we're talking about 4% each

231
00:15:34,063 --> 00:15:35,770
4% goes to Allah,

232
00:15:35,850 --> 00:15:37,492
4% goes to Rasool Ullah,

233
00:15:37,555 --> 00:15:39,687
4% goes to the near relatives,

234
00:15:40,277 --> 00:15:42,065
4% goes to the orphans,

235
00:15:42,247 --> 00:15:44,620
4% goes to the poor

236
00:15:44,715 --> 00:15:47,953
and 4% goes to the traveler.

237
00:15:48,845 --> 00:15:58,542
Now the portion that goes to Allah and Rasool Allah ﷺ is distributed in what is needed by the Muslims,

238
00:15:58,836 --> 00:16:01,646
 such as Masajid(مساجد) or paving roads or whatever,

239
00:16:01,897 --> 00:16:05,782
it is up to the Imam(إمام) of the Muslims to distribute that.

240
00:16:06,889 --> 00:16:11,610
So, these are the rulings regarding the distribution of the booty.

241
00:16:13,478 --> 00:16:17,634
Another issue dealt with in the Ayaat(آيات) of Surat-Al-Anfaal(سورة الأنفال),

242
00:16:17,832 --> 00:16:19,173
the prisoners of war.

243
00:16:19,966 --> 00:16:22,633
Rasool Allah ﷺ has 70 prisoners of war.

244
00:16:22,815 --> 00:16:25,159
So, he invites the Sahabah for Shura(شورى),

245
00:16:25,964 --> 00:16:28,961
and he hears various opinions.

246
00:16:30,154 --> 00:16:34,631
Abu Bakr Siddique رضي الله عنه speaks, and his opinion was;

247
00:16:35,052 --> 00:16:44,068
O Messenger of Allah, These are our relatives, these are our tribe ask for ransom.

248
00:16:44,354 --> 00:16:48,529
 This ransom will strengthen us, it will strengthen Islam

249
00:16:48,847 --> 00:16:51,059
and maybe these people will become Muslim.

250
00:16:51,248 --> 00:16:53,564
So, that was the opinion of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر).

251
00:16:54,027 --> 00:16:58,373
He says; O, Messenger of Allah, they are your people, your relatives,

252
00:16:58,699 --> 00:17:03,357
let them live, be lenient to them, perhaps Allah will forgive them.

253
00:17:04,075 --> 00:17:05,032
Umar Bin Khattab(عمر بن خطاب) said;

254
00:17:05,072 --> 00:17:11,304
O Messenger of Allah, they exiled you and called you a liar, bring them close and strike their necks.

255
00:17:11,737 --> 00:17:14,012
This was the opinion of Umar(عُمَر).

256
00:17:14,988 --> 00:17:17,985
In another narration, it says, Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) said;

257
00:17:18,444 --> 00:17:22,072
O Messenger of Allah, these are your close relatives, your tribal brothers,

258
00:17:22,294 --> 00:17:24,411
 I think you should accept ransom from them,

259
00:17:24,680 --> 00:17:28,649
what we receive from them will give us power against the unbelievers

260
00:17:28,729 --> 00:17:34,030
 and Allah might well give them guidance so that they become allied to us.

261
00:17:34,391 --> 00:17:37,665
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: I don't agree with Abu Bakr(ابو بكر),

262
00:17:37,937 --> 00:17:40,770
I think you should hand over to me so and so

263
00:17:41,217 --> 00:17:44,949
referring to one of his relatives, and I'll strike his neck.

264
00:17:45,539 --> 00:17:48,719
And you hand over Aqeel(عقيل) to his brother Ali(علي).

265
00:17:48,926 --> 00:17:50,242
 So, he can strike his neck

266
00:17:50,627 --> 00:17:54,933
and you hand over to Hamza(حمزه) so and so, his brother, so he can strike his neck.

267
00:17:55,352 --> 00:18:01,306
That way Allah will know that we feel no leniency towards the Mushrikeen(مشركين).

268
00:18:01,632 --> 00:18:05,928
These men are their chieftains, their very leaders.

269
00:18:07,128 --> 00:18:11,101
And in another narration Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة) spoke,

270
00:18:11,754 --> 00:18:15,189
And he said, I suggest, O Messenger of Allah

271
00:18:15,598 --> 00:18:20,638
you find the valley with many trees, make them enter it and then set them on fire.

272
00:18:20,960 --> 00:18:25,434
 You burn them in that valley, that was the opinion of Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة).

273
00:18:26,323 --> 00:18:29,693
Rasool Allah ﷺ went in, and then it came out

274
00:18:30,256 --> 00:18:33,115
And Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

275
00:18:33,658 --> 00:18:37,385
Allah softens the hearts of men concerning Him

276
00:18:37,813 --> 00:18:40,043
so that they become softer than soft,

277
00:18:40,594 --> 00:18:42,951
and Allah hardens the hearts of men

278
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:45,666
so that they become harder than stone.

279
00:18:46,355 --> 00:18:48,609
You Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) are like Ibrahim(ابراهيم) who said;

280
00:18:48,977 --> 00:18:50,880
Whoever follows me, is of me

281
00:18:51,186 --> 00:18:54,902
and whoever disobeys me then you are Forgiving and Merciful.

282
00:18:55,542 --> 00:18:57,695
You Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) are like Jesus, who said;

283
00:18:58,109 --> 00:19:00,611
If You punish them, they are Your servants.

284
00:19:00,897 --> 00:19:04,841
If You forgive them, then You are the all powerful and Wise.

285
00:19:05,148 --> 00:19:09,046
So, the analogy of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), he is similar to Ibrahim(ابراهيم) and Eesa(عيسى),

286
00:19:09,308 --> 00:19:11,109
 who were lenient, with their people.

287
00:19:12,243 --> 00:19:15,246
You Umar(عُمَر) are like Noah(نوح), who said, O Lord,

288
00:19:15,345 --> 00:19:18,619
Do not leave on the earth any place for the unbelievers.

289
00:19:19,417 --> 00:19:25,206
Noah(نوح) made a Dua(دُعَا) to Allahعَزّوجَلّ to obliterate, to destroy all of the Kuffar(كفار).

290
00:19:26,107 --> 00:19:29,197
And Umar you are like Musa(موسى), who said;

291
00:19:29,292 --> 00:19:33,525
O Allah, destroy their wealth and make their hearts hard,

292
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:37,612
for they will not believe, until they see the painful punishment.

293
00:19:38,359 --> 00:19:39,768
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

294
00:19:39,847 --> 00:19:44,402
Let none be exempt from either ransom or having their head smitten.

295
00:19:45,256 --> 00:19:51,019
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was inclined to adopt the opinion of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر),

296
00:19:51,676 --> 00:19:54,591
and he was willing to accept ransom.

297
00:19:55,239 --> 00:19:59,887
One Day, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) comes out and sees that Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) were crying.

298
00:20:00,391 --> 00:20:02,524
Actually, the following day,

299
00:20:02,863 --> 00:20:03,441
Umar(عُمَر) said;

300
00:20:03,521 --> 00:20:06,362
I went to the Prophet ﷺ early in the morning

301
00:20:06,821 --> 00:20:08,612
He was with Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) and they were weeping,

302
00:20:08,652 --> 00:20:13,224
 I asked: O, Messenger of Allah tell me, why you and your companion are weeping?

303
00:20:13,401 --> 00:20:19,135
If I find the reason to weep, I'll do so, if I don't I'll pretend to weep at your weeping.

304
00:20:19,983 --> 00:20:21,325
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

305
00:20:21,468 --> 00:20:27,590
I am weeping at how your companions proposed to me that I accept ransom.

306
00:20:28,067 --> 00:20:31,201
Your punishment for doing so, was proposed to me,

307
00:20:31,357 --> 00:20:33,213
and it was closer than this tree.

308
00:20:33,924 --> 00:20:37,626
Meaning Allahعَزّوجَلّ wasn't happy that the Muslims accepted ransom.

309
00:20:37,833 --> 00:20:38,507
Why.?

310
00:20:38,587 --> 00:20:45,559
Allahعَزّوجَلّ revealed the Ayaat(آيات) Sixty seven To 69 Surat-Al-Anfaal(سورة الأنفال)

311
00:20:46,155 --> 00:20:47,512
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

312
00:20:48,065 --> 00:20:56,353
مَا كَانَ لِنَبِيٍّ أَنْ يَكُونَ لَهُ أَسْرَىٰ حَتَّىٰ يُثْخِنَ فِي الْأَرْضِ ۚ

313
00:20:57,018 --> 00:21:06,068
تُرِيدُونَ عَرَضَ الدُّنْيَا وَاللَّهُ يُرِيدُ الْآخِرَةَ ۗ وَاللَّهُ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ۝

314
00:21:06,505 --> 00:21:16,308
لَوْلَا كِتَابٌ مِنَ اللَّهِ سَبَقَ لَمَسَّكُمْ فِيمَا أَخَذْتُمْ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٌ۝

315
00:21:17,157 --> 00:21:21,052
It is not for a Prophet to have captives of war,

316
00:21:21,288 --> 00:21:25,941
until he inflicts a massacre upon Allah's enemies in the land.

317
00:21:26,657 --> 00:21:32,227
You i.e. some Muslims desire the commodities of this world.

318
00:21:32,500 --> 00:21:37,981
But Allah desires for you the hereafter and Allah is Exalted and Might and Wise.

319
00:21:38,421 --> 00:21:41,330
If not for a decree from Allah that preceded,

320
00:21:41,536 --> 00:21:44,944
you would have been touched for what you took by great punishment.

321
00:21:45,024 --> 00:21:45,913
Two things in these Ayaat(آيات).

322
00:21:45,953 --> 00:21:46,825
Number one;

323
00:21:47,385 --> 00:21:50,103
Rasool Allah ﷺ should have executed them all.

324
00:21:50,422 --> 00:21:56,932
That is what would have pleased Allahعَزّوجَلّ, to execute all of these prisoners.

325
00:21:57,484 --> 00:21:58,138
Why.?

326
00:21:58,249 --> 00:21:59,408
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

327
00:21:59,599 --> 00:22:06,424
It is not for Prophet to have captives of war, until he inflicts a slaughter upon Allah's enemies in the land.

328
00:22:07,042 --> 00:22:15,475
 A newly forming state, Jama'ah(جماعة) needs to show its strength in the beginning.

329
00:22:16,156 --> 00:22:26,017
And asking for ransom here, is less of a strong opinion compared to the execution of all of those prisoners.

330
00:22:26,142 --> 00:22:30,282
However, Allahعَزّوجَلّ says in the following Ayaat(آيات) that

331
00:22:30,854 --> 00:22:36,461
if it was not for a decree that proceeded from Allah you would have been touched by punishment.

332
00:22:36,636 --> 00:22:39,314
 Allah has made asking for ransom Halal(حلال)

333
00:22:39,490 --> 00:22:41,420
And Allah has made Ghaneema(غنيمه) Halal(حلال).

334
00:22:41,660 --> 00:22:46,242
Therefore what the Muslims did was allowed, otherwise they would have been punished.

335
00:22:47,115 --> 00:22:49,742
 So, I hope that this issue is clear.

336
00:22:51,572 --> 00:22:53,080
Mujahid Ath-Thori(مجاهد ألثوري) say;

337
00:22:53,159 --> 00:22:57,848
were it not for a decree from Allah that came previously that is in forgiving them,

338
00:22:57,975 --> 00:23:00,512
 while the majority opinion as Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) states

339
00:23:00,739 --> 00:23:03,550
is that it is the allowing of Ghaneema(غنيمه) and ransom.

340
00:23:03,699 --> 00:23:06,261
So what Rasool Allah ﷺ did was allowed.

341
00:23:06,666 --> 00:23:11,104
However, it would have been better, if ransom was not accepted,

342
00:23:11,303 --> 00:23:13,463
 and these prisoners were executed.

343
00:23:15,470 --> 00:23:26,407
Rasool Allah ﷺ as we mentioned, was employing the method of formal ranks in the battlefield,

344
00:23:27,084 --> 00:23:36,001
rather than the method of the Arab warfare which was to attack and withdraw, in a not a very organized manner.

345
00:23:36,809 --> 00:23:39,704
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was straightening the lines,

346
00:23:40,485 --> 00:23:43,383
as if he was straightening the lines for prayer.

347
00:23:44,260 --> 00:23:46,661
And he was holding an arrow in his hand.

348
00:23:46,986 --> 00:23:52,459
And he came up to one of the soldiers, Sawad Bin Ghuzaiyya(سوادبن غزية),

349
00:23:53,013 --> 00:23:56,038
who was protruding a bit from the line.

350
00:23:56,331 --> 00:24:00,511
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ pushes him back with the arrow

351
00:24:00,989 --> 00:24:04,666
sort of like with the arrow in his stomach, he pushes him back.

352
00:24:05,495 --> 00:24:06,991
So, Sawad Bin Ghuzaiyya(سواد بن غزية) says,

353
00:24:07,048 --> 00:24:10,546
O Rasool Ullah, You hurt me, I want to retaliate.

354
00:24:11,060 --> 00:24:15,356
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), Sawad(سواد) this is right before the battle,

355
00:24:15,792 --> 00:24:21,156
and you say to Rasool Allah ﷺ that I want to retaliate, just because he hurt you.

356
00:24:22,437 --> 00:24:25,553
Rasool Allah ﷺ, What was his response?

357
00:24:26,482 --> 00:24:30,493
You know, here one of his soldier is saying that you hurt me, I want to retaliate now.

358
00:24:30,939 --> 00:24:34,652
It's your mistake, Sawad(سواد), Why Weren't you standing straight in the line...

359
00:24:35,820 --> 00:24:39,499
But Rasool Allah ﷺ exposed his stomach

360
00:24:40,303 --> 00:24:42,173
and said go ahead and retaliate.

361
00:24:42,379 --> 00:24:44,979
If that's what you want. Go ahead.

362
00:24:45,577 --> 00:24:48,067
Rasool Allah ﷺ, did not get angry, he didn't get upset.

363
00:24:48,464 --> 00:24:52,057
He didn't order his soldiers to take Sawad(سواد)

364
00:24:52,131 --> 00:24:55,806
and court Marshal him, and throw him in jail, torture him

365
00:24:56,265 --> 00:25:03,774
because he spoke insuch a fashion to the leader of the army, disobey the direct military order.

366
00:25:04,150 --> 00:25:08,287
Rasool Allah ﷺ exposed his stomach and told him; Sawad(سواد) go ahead and retaliate.

367
00:25:08,763 --> 00:25:11,454
If I hurt you, Go ahead and retaliate.

368
00:25:12,279 --> 00:25:18,842
So, Sawad Bin Ghuzaiyya رضي الله عنه hugs Rasool Allah ﷺ and he kisses his stomach.

369
00:25:19,858 --> 00:25:21,267
That was his retaliation.

370
00:25:21,805 --> 00:25:23,378
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Sawad:

371
00:25:23,418 --> 00:25:24,933
   مَا حَمَلَكَ عَلَى مَا صَنَعَتْ

372
00:25:24,973 --> 00:25:26,129
Why did he do that?

373
00:25:26,488 --> 00:25:29,467
Sawad Bin Ghuzaiyya(سواد بن غزية) said: O Messenger of Allah

374
00:25:29,906 --> 00:25:32,150
You can see what is about to happen.

375
00:25:32,547 --> 00:25:37,267
I wanted my last contact with you to be my skin touching yours.

376
00:25:37,913 --> 00:25:39,428
  لا اله الا الله

377
00:25:40,165 --> 00:25:41,976
Sawad Bin Ghuzaiyya(سواد بن غزية) is saying;

378
00:25:42,016 --> 00:25:47,139
O Messenger of Allah, you can see what is about to happen, I might die in a few moments in a few hours.

379
00:25:48,172 --> 00:25:50,297
We're facing death right in front of us.

380
00:25:50,964 --> 00:25:55,447
I wanted the last thing in this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) to be, my skin touching yours.

381
00:25:56,454 --> 00:25:59,154
This is how they loved Rasool Allah ﷺ

382
00:26:00,039 --> 00:26:03,979
Sawad Bin Ghuzaiyya(سواد بن غزية), who was hurt by Rasool Allah ﷺ accidentally,

383
00:26:04,469 --> 00:26:10,471
used this opportunity to kiss Rasool Allah ﷺ and to hug him.

384
00:26:11,727 --> 00:26:14,933
They didn't see it, that Rasool Allah ﷺ was leading them to their death.

385
00:26:15,026 --> 00:26:21,113
 They didn't see it that they're suffering all of this troubled because of him and because of his Da'wah(دعوة).

386
00:26:21,693 --> 00:26:30,117
 They were willingly going ahead to face death, for the sake of Allahعَزّوجَلّ

387
00:26:30,839 --> 00:26:34,495
and His Servant and Messenger, Muhammadﷺ.

388
00:26:35,594 --> 00:26:40,992
Rasool Allah ﷺ then makes Dua(دُعَا) for Sawad(سواد), that may Allahعَزّوجَلّ bless him.

389
00:26:42,230 --> 00:26:46,438
It is this love of Rasool Allah ﷺ that we want to learn from these series,

390
00:26:47,368 --> 00:26:51,288
how the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم understood the meaning

391
00:26:51,328 --> 00:26:54,331
 and the concept of loving Muhammadﷺ,

392
00:26:54,616 --> 00:27:02,462
what it meant to them, it wasn't just words on their tongues, poetry, singing his praise,

393
00:27:03,145 --> 00:27:08,107
love for them meant that we'll put everything on the line for you.

394
00:27:08,907 --> 00:27:15,857
Everything will lay it down for you, O Messenger of Allah, our wealth, our money, our family, our children.

395
00:27:16,230 --> 00:27:22,730
Everything is sacrificeable when it comes to you, we're willing to give everything up.

396
00:27:23,861 --> 00:27:27,734
We ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to grant us this love of Muhammadﷺ,

397
00:27:27,774 --> 00:27:31,107
the love of his message, the loveof his Sunnah, the love of his way.

398
00:27:32,077 --> 00:27:37,017
And not just to make us people, who claim that they love him and pay it lip service.

399
00:27:37,811 --> 00:27:40,452
And we asked Allahعَزّوجَلّ to make us love His Shariah(شريعه)

400
00:27:40,492 --> 00:27:42,247
 and Allahعَزّوجَلّ says in Qur'an,

401
00:27:42,642 --> 00:27:44,603
And this something he granted the Shahabah

402
00:27:45,070 --> 00:27:48,032
حَبَّبَ إِلَيْكُمُ الْإِيمَانَ وَزَيَّنَهُ فِي قُلُوبِكُمْ

403
00:27:48,492 --> 00:27:52,601
He made you a love Eeman(ايمان) and made it adorned in your hearts.

404
00:27:53,408 --> 00:27:55,678
So, for them Eeman(ايمان) was something that they loved.

405
00:27:56,316 --> 00:27:58,265
And Rasool Allah ﷺ says inthe Hadith(حديث),

406
00:27:58,622 --> 00:28:02,525
you're not going to taste the sweetness of Eeman(إيمان), until one of three things.

407
00:28:02,823 --> 00:28:07,223
One of them is that you would dislike going back to Kuffr(كفر) like you would dislike being thrown in fire.

408
00:28:08,455 --> 00:28:15,050
So, you'd love Eeman(إيمان), so much that you would rather be thrown in fire to burn in fire, than to give it up.

409
00:28:15,160 --> 00:28:17,492
You love your Eeman(إيمان), you love your Islam so much

410
00:28:17,563 --> 00:28:21,508
that is when you would really taste the sweetness of Eeman(إيمان).

411
00:28:22,591 --> 00:28:28,629
 Rasool Allah ﷺ after he did his best in terms of preparation

412
00:28:30,043 --> 00:28:31,896
in terms of arranging the army,

413
00:28:32,261 --> 00:28:34,221
in terms of choosing the location

414
00:28:35,124 --> 00:28:37,751
in terms of making Shura(شورى),

415
00:28:38,338 --> 00:28:43,028
when he exhausted all of the worldly means, what did he do next?

416
00:28:43,926 --> 00:28:49,709
The next thing he did, is put his trust in Allahعَزّوجَلّ and Make Dua(دُعَا).

417
00:28:51,001 --> 00:28:55,469
Dear brothers and sisters, This is what Tawakkul(توكل) means,

418
00:28:56,379 --> 00:29:03,476
it means that you do the best in terms of the worldly means, you exhaust them to the limit.

419
00:29:04,420 --> 00:29:10,147
And then after that you throw the matter into the hands of Allahعَزّوجَلّ, you leave it to Him.

420
00:29:11,589 --> 00:29:19,292
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ now, after he did his best, he went a side, and he raised his hands.

421
00:29:19,794 --> 00:29:21,177
And he started making Dua(دُعَا).

422
00:29:22,071 --> 00:29:24,256
 And he was so involved in that Dua(دُعَا).

423
00:29:25,208 --> 00:29:32,507
And it took him so long, and he was saying, O Allah, I appeal to your pact and to your oath.

424
00:29:33,328 --> 00:29:36,758
If you wish it, you will not be worshiped ever again, after this day.

425
00:29:37,692 --> 00:29:42,321
Because this is it, these are the Muslims, if they're killed who will worship You.

426
00:29:43,232 --> 00:29:45,759
And he went on and on making Dua(دُعَا) to Allahعَزّوجَلّ

427
00:29:45,811 --> 00:29:48,327
and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) was feeling sorry for Muhammadﷺ,

428
00:29:48,367 --> 00:29:49,573
he went to him and he said;

429
00:29:49,898 --> 00:29:51,160
he held him by the hand and said;

430
00:29:51,200 --> 00:29:54,550
that's enough O Messenger of Allah, it's enough of asking Your Lord.

431
00:29:55,106 --> 00:29:57,288
Now the reason why Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) said that,

432
00:29:57,433 --> 00:29:59,217
I'm quoting Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر)

433
00:29:59,546 --> 00:30:03,058
he said, by saying these words, he was in a fact asking

434
00:30:03,966 --> 00:30:06,768
Why are you so exhausting yourself?

435
00:30:07,798 --> 00:30:10,518
Allah has made you a promise of help.

436
00:30:11,786 --> 00:30:19,779
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), Allah bless him, was a tender hearted man, with great empathy, and compassion for the Messenger of Allah.

437
00:30:20,850 --> 00:30:29,220
Rasool Allah ﷺ, then went outside of his portico walking vigorously in his armor,

438
00:30:29,575 --> 00:30:33,073
 speaking the verse, the force will be defeated.

439
00:30:33,542 --> 00:30:38,010
They will retreat, the hour will come and it will be most bitter.

440
00:30:38,690 --> 00:30:43,061
سَيُهْزَمُ الْجَمْعُ وَيُوَلُّونَ الدُّبُرَ۝

441
00:30:43,236 --> 00:30:49,178
بَلِالسَّاعَةُ مَوْعِدُهُمْ وَالسَّاعَةُ أَدْهَىٰ وَأَمَرُّ۝

442
00:30:50,022 --> 00:30:55,765
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ has promised Rasool Allah ﷺ victory after his long Dua(دُعَا)

443
00:30:55,853 --> 00:30:58,237
 Allah (عَزّوجَلّ) says, in Surat-Al-Anfaal(سورة الأنفال)

444
00:30:58,696 --> 00:31:11,109
إِذْ تَسْتَغِيثُونَ رَبَّكُمْ فَاسْتَجَابَ لَكُمْ أَنِّي مُمِدُّكُمْ بِأَلْفٍ مِنَ الْمَلَائِكَةِ مُرْدِفِينَ۝

445
00:31:11,309 --> 00:31:13,806
Remember when you asked help of your Lord.

446
00:31:14,060 --> 00:31:20,904
 And He answered you indeed I will reinforce you with 1000 from the angels following one another.

447
00:31:20,959 --> 00:31:25,555
 So, this was the response that came back to Rasool Allah ﷺ after his Dua(دُعَا),

448
00:31:26,007 --> 00:31:29,223
 I am sending you 1000 angels.

449
00:31:30,286 --> 00:31:33,056
Now one Angel would be enough.

450
00:31:33,346 --> 00:31:39,001
We know that Jibril عليه السّلام destroyed the people of loot(لوط) with the tip of his wing.

451
00:31:39,829 --> 00:31:41,993
So, one angel is enough why 1000.

452
00:31:42,543 --> 00:31:46,630
Well, the point here is to give comfort to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

453
00:31:47,187 --> 00:31:49,014
It's not one angel or two Angel,

454
00:31:49,061 --> 00:31:53,846
 I mean Allah(عَزّوجَلّ) with  كن فيكون can destroy the entire army.

455
00:31:54,216 --> 00:31:56,826
But here Allahعَزّوجَلّ is giving Tathbeet(تثبيت),

456
00:31:57,256 --> 00:32:00,485
is giving comfort to the Muslims and steadfastness

457
00:32:01,395 --> 00:32:03,445
and Allahعَزّوجَلّ says,

458
00:32:03,855 --> 00:32:09,005
فَلَمْ تَقْتُلُوهُمْ وَلَٰكِنَّ اللَّهَ قَتَلَهُمْ ۚ

459
00:32:09,259 --> 00:32:14,777
وَمَا رَمَيْتَ إِذْ رَمَيْتَ وَلَٰكِنَّ اللَّهَ رَمَىٰ

460
00:32:15,189 --> 00:32:20,570
وَلِيُبْلِيَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ مِنْهُ بَلَاءً حَسَنًا

461
00:32:20,800 --> 00:32:24,938
إِنَّ اللَّهَ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ۝

462
00:32:25,492 --> 00:32:28,125
And you did not kill them, but it was Allah, who killed them.

463
00:32:28,540 --> 00:32:32,988
And you threw not O Muhammad(محمد), when you threw but it was Allah, Who threw

464
00:32:33,246 --> 00:32:37,393
that he might test the believers with a good test, indeed Allah is hearing and Knowing.

465
00:32:38,232 --> 00:32:38,925
Now here,

466
00:32:39,210 --> 00:32:40,401
وَمَا رَمَيْتَ إِذْ رَمَيْتَ

467
00:32:40,458 --> 00:32:45,035
You did not throw when you threw but it was Allah, Who threw.

468
00:32:45,408 --> 00:32:51,101
This could apply to any situation of war, where a Muslim is fighting his enemy.

469
00:32:51,310 --> 00:32:57,648
However, the scholars of Tafseer(تفسير) mention a specific incident after which this Ayaah(آية) was revealed.

470
00:32:57,688 --> 00:33:03,952
 And that is, they say that Rasool Allahﷺ held in his hand, some sand or dirt,

471
00:33:04,325 --> 00:33:08,662
and he threw it, towards the enemies of Allahعَزّوجَلّ

472
00:33:09,177 --> 00:33:16,301
and one particle of that sand flew into the face or the eye of every one of the disbelievers.

473
00:33:16,515 --> 00:33:19,024
 And that is when Allah(عَزّوجَلّ) revealed this verse,

474
00:33:19,425 --> 00:33:24,913
And you threw not O Muhammad(محمد), when you threw, but it was Allah(عَزّوجَلّ) who threw.

475
00:33:25,890 --> 00:33:34,279
Al-Aswad Al-Makhzoomi(ألأسود ألمخذومي) was an evil, bad character man from the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

476
00:33:34,779 --> 00:33:40,840
 He made an oath, he said I'm gonna reach to the wells and drink from them.

477
00:33:41,500 --> 00:33:46,267
And we already said that the wells now were under the control of the Muslims.

478
00:33:47,049 --> 00:33:51,046
So, he marches forth, to go towards the wells

479
00:33:51,516 --> 00:33:58,653
and Hamza رضي الله عنه jumps forth and strikes his leg.

480
00:33:58,837 --> 00:34:03,266
 So it came off and Al-Aswad(الاسود) fell on his back

481
00:34:03,347 --> 00:34:08,737
with his leg in the air spurting blood towards the army of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

482
00:34:09,309 --> 00:34:17,286
 But he was so stubborn, he continued crawling in order to fulfill his oath and reach the wells

483
00:34:17,659 --> 00:34:21,628
but Hamza Bin Abdul-Muttalib(حمزه بن عبدالمطلب) struck him again, until he killed him.

484
00:34:22,354 --> 00:34:24,798
Now whether this was the first person to die,

485
00:34:25,052 --> 00:34:30,670
or it was the three men who came out for single combat Allah Ho Alam(الله اعلم).

486
00:34:30,939 --> 00:34:33,747
Anyway, Ut'ba Bin Rabiyah(عتبة بن ربيعة)

487
00:34:34,405 --> 00:34:36,769
and his son Al-Waleed Bin Ut'ba(الوليدبن عتبة)

488
00:34:37,119 --> 00:34:45,318
and his brother Shaibah(شيبة), the three of them, stood in front of their army

489
00:34:46,064 --> 00:34:51,099
 and challenged the Muslims for single combat, dueling.

490
00:34:52,016 --> 00:34:56,646
Ut'ba(عتبة) and his brother Shaibah(شيبة) and Ut'ba(عتبة)'s son, Al-Waleed(الوليد)

491
00:34:57,290 --> 00:35:01,050
So, the three men are now standing in front of the army of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

492
00:35:01,539 --> 00:35:05,689
and they're facing the Muslims and challenging them for single combat,

493
00:35:06,334 --> 00:35:08,751
Mubaridha(مبارزه), what is called Mubaridha(مبارزه), dueling.

494
00:35:10,009 --> 00:35:14,234
Three young men from among the Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار) jumped forth

495
00:35:14,817 --> 00:35:17,167
Auf(عوف) and Muawwiz Ibn Afrah(معوذ إبن أفرع)

496
00:35:17,339 --> 00:35:18,627
and Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة)

497
00:35:19,124 --> 00:35:20,952
And these were all three young men.

498
00:35:21,640 --> 00:35:22,852
When they approached Ut'ba(عتبة),

499
00:35:22,939 --> 00:35:24,304
 Ut'ba(عتبة) said: Who are you?

500
00:35:24,479 --> 00:35:25,662
Introduce yourselves.

501
00:35:26,066 --> 00:35:27,210
So, they introduce themselves.

502
00:35:27,250 --> 00:35:29,317
He said: Worthy opponents,

503
00:35:29,577 --> 00:35:35,542
however we want to meet our peers from among our own people.

504
00:35:36,338 --> 00:35:41,866
Ut'ba(عتبة) is saying to these men, that we have no quarrel with you

505
00:35:42,607 --> 00:35:46,715
you know, our problem is not with Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار), our problem is not with Al-Aos Wal-Khazraj(ألأوس ولخزرج)

506
00:35:46,902 --> 00:35:54,131
 our problem are with the men of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), who followed Muhammadﷺ,

507
00:35:54,517 --> 00:36:00,023
so send us, our peers, people equivalent of our status.

508
00:36:01,168 --> 00:36:03,938
Now, Ut'ba Bin Rabiyah(عتبة بن ربيعة) was one of the leaders of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

509
00:36:04,071 --> 00:36:08,658
he was part of the nobility of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and he comes out with his brother and his son.

510
00:36:08,853 --> 00:36:10,462
And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) just remember that

511
00:36:10,938 --> 00:36:14,794
a while ago it was Ut'ba(عتبة), who was calling the kuffar(كفار) to go back.

512
00:36:15,400 --> 00:36:20,661
But Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) is the one, who inspired them and fired up, this army to fight

513
00:36:20,942 --> 00:36:25,940
and he cornered Ut'ba(عتبة) by accusing him, of being a coward,

514
00:36:26,012 --> 00:36:29,821
 so now Ut'ba(عتبة) is trying to prove that he's not the coward,

515
00:36:30,507 --> 00:36:32,989
 and that he's not afraid of meeting the Muslims

516
00:36:33,061 --> 00:36:37,283
because his own son might end up being killed, his son Hudaifah(حديفه)

517
00:36:37,882 --> 00:36:43,059
his stubbornness ended up leading him, to this situation that he was in.

518
00:36:44,036 --> 00:36:46,734
Now Al-Ammawwi(ألأموي), one of the scholars of Seerah(سيرة),

519
00:36:46,774 --> 00:36:50,723
he says that Rasool Allah ﷺ wasn't happy

520
00:36:51,238 --> 00:36:55,365
that three men from among Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار), the ones who responded to the challenge.

521
00:36:55,661 --> 00:37:00,187
Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted his own relatives, his own family to go out.

522
00:37:00,590 --> 00:37:02,682
So, when Ut'ba(عتبة) send the men back,

523
00:37:02,893 --> 00:37:04,004
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

524
00:37:04,136 --> 00:37:07,465
قم يا حمزه' قم يا عبيده'قم يا علي

525
00:37:07,888 --> 00:37:09,634
O Hamza(حمزه), stand up

526
00:37:10,020 --> 00:37:11,935
O Obaidah(عبيدة) stand up,

527
00:37:12,332 --> 00:37:13,999
and O Ali(علي) stand up.

528
00:37:14,228 --> 00:37:19,195
 Now, Obaidah(عبيده) here is Obaidah Bin Hariss(عبيدة بن حارث), the cousin of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

529
00:37:19,235 --> 00:37:21,421
 Obaidah Bin Hariss Bin Abdul Muttalib(عبيدة بن حارث بن عبدالمطلب).

530
00:37:21,932 --> 00:37:25,061
So, he's the direct cousin of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

531
00:37:25,907 --> 00:37:29,351
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is asking these three men to go forth.

532
00:37:29,631 --> 00:37:32,529
Now, Rasool Allah ﷺ as Al-Ammawwi(ألأموي) says, wasn't happy

533
00:37:32,579 --> 00:37:46,792
 because you see, this is the first time, the Muslims and the Mushrikeen(مشركين) are standing face to face in battle.

534
00:37:47,388 --> 00:37:49,254
We had skirmishes before this

535
00:37:49,659 --> 00:37:55,843
but this is the first time, where they would face off each other in single combat.

536
00:37:56,704 --> 00:38:00,179
So by no means, was this an insignificant event.

537
00:38:00,204 --> 00:38:02,156
This was a very significant event.

538
00:38:02,214 --> 00:38:04,470
This Mubaridha(مبارزه) is extremely significant.

539
00:38:05,425 --> 00:38:07,558
In fact, Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) says,

540
00:38:07,616 --> 00:38:18,401
I will be the first person who kneels before Allahعَزّوجَلّ, the Almighty among the adversaries on Judgment Day.

541
00:38:18,805 --> 00:38:20,508
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) is saying that

542
00:38:20,869 --> 00:38:25,850
I will be the first one to kneel in front of Allahعَزّوجَلّ on the Day of Judgment.

543
00:38:26,224 --> 00:38:30,385
When Allah will judge among Al-Mukhtasimeen(ألمختَصِمين), among the adversaries

544
00:38:30,886 --> 00:38:33,420
among the people who disputed in this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

545
00:38:34,108 --> 00:38:38,173
Because these three men from among Al-Mushriqeen(ألمشركين)

546
00:38:38,787 --> 00:38:42,061
and their equivalent, from among Muslimeen(ألمسلمين)

547
00:38:42,488 --> 00:38:46,061
are not facing off and fighting over land,

548
00:38:46,723 --> 00:38:49,242
they're not fighting over wealth,

549
00:38:49,815 --> 00:38:52,537
they're not fighting over power or dominance.

550
00:38:53,017 --> 00:38:54,864
They are fighting over their Lord.

551
00:38:55,328 --> 00:38:58,656
 So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ revealed in Surat Ul-Hajj(سوره الحج)

552
00:38:59,080 --> 00:39:02,439
هَٰذَانِ خَصْمَانِ اخْتَصَمُوا فِي رَبِّهِمْ ۖ

553
00:39:03,200 --> 00:39:08,018
These are two adversaries, who have disputed over their Lord.

554
00:39:08,298 --> 00:39:11,033
And the scholars of Tafseer(تفسير) say, that this Ayaah(آية)

555
00:39:11,130 --> 00:39:15,631
is talking about the Mubaridha(مبارزه), the dueling that happened on the day of Badr(بدر).

556
00:39:16,769 --> 00:39:19,645
So, Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب), Hamza(حمزه) and Obaidah(عبيدة)

557
00:39:20,191 --> 00:39:25,728
they rush ahead to face off with Ut'ba(عتبة), Shaibah(شيبة) and Al-Waleed(الوليد).

558
00:39:26,626 --> 00:39:32,528
Obaidah(عبيدة) was the eldest among them, he was the senior, so he faced off with Ut'ba(عتبة),

559
00:39:33,058 --> 00:39:36,628
since Ut'ba(عتبة) was the oldest from among the three Mushrikeen(مشركين)

560
00:39:37,406 --> 00:39:41,386
and Ali(علي) stood in front of Al-Waleed(الوليد).

561
00:39:41,681 --> 00:39:46,235
And These were the two youngest and then Hamza(حمزه) in front of Shaibah(شيبة).

562
00:39:47,426 --> 00:39:53,860
And they started battle, and dust was just erupting from beneath their feet.

563
00:39:55,045 --> 00:40:00,403
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) and Hamza(حمزه) immediately killed their opponents.

564
00:40:01,474 --> 00:40:09,394
But Ut'ba(عتبة) and Obaidah(عبيدة) both exchanged blows, and both of them fell down,

565
00:40:09,878 --> 00:40:13,875
but they were incapable of carrying on the fight, however, they were not dead.

566
00:40:14,232 --> 00:40:17,790
Each one of them, hurt the other one with a blow

567
00:40:18,244 --> 00:40:23,606
but they couldn't carry on the fight and the same time they were both still alive.

568
00:40:24,547 --> 00:40:28,310
Ali(علي) and Hamza(حمزه) then attacked Ut'ba(عتبة) and killed him and Ali(علي) says,

569
00:40:28,513 --> 00:40:31,774
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not reprimand us for that,

570
00:40:31,833 --> 00:40:35,072
meaning that, it was an acceptable thing to do in a duel.

571
00:40:36,027 --> 00:40:39,816
And then they carried Obaidah(عبيدة) back to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

572
00:40:40,573 --> 00:40:43,320
This was the first Mubaridha(مبارزه) in Islam.

573
00:40:43,963 --> 00:40:51,591
And therefore Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) will be the first to kneel in front of Allahعَزّوجَلّ on the Day of Judgment,

574
00:40:51,945 --> 00:40:54,782
when Allahعَزّوجَلّ will judge among the people, who dispute.

575
00:40:55,929 --> 00:40:59,054
And this could also apply to Hamza(حمزه) and Obaidah(عبيدة).

576
00:41:00,063 --> 00:41:02,339
They carried back Obaidah Bin Hariss(عبيدة بن حارث)

577
00:41:03,315 --> 00:41:10,655
and Rasool Allah ﷺ honored him by placing his head on the thigh of Rasool Allah ﷺ

578
00:41:11,473 --> 00:41:15,140
Abu Talib(ابو طالب), the uncle of Rasool Ullah would say,

579
00:41:15,393 --> 00:41:26,968
we will serve the Messenger of Allah, until we are laid out before him uncaring even, of our sons and our wives.

580
00:41:27,490 --> 00:41:29,039
Abu Talib(ابو طالب) was saying that

581
00:41:29,516 --> 00:41:32,269
we will serve Rasool Allah ﷺ

582
00:41:32,786 --> 00:41:39,363
and we will lay before him our sons, and our wives, and our lives, for him.

583
00:41:39,973 --> 00:41:49,038
Obaidah Bin Hariss رضي الله عنه said, to Rasool Allah ﷺ while he was laying on Rasool Allah ﷺ, on his lap.

584
00:41:49,901 --> 00:41:54,852
He said; O Messenger of Allah, If Abu Talib(ابو طالب) could only see me,

585
00:41:55,378 --> 00:41:58,553
he would know that it wasto me, his words applied.

586
00:41:59,070 --> 00:42:05,811
We will serve him until, we are laid out before him, uncaring even of our sons and our wives.

587
00:42:06,182 --> 00:42:07,926
And this was narrated by Ash-Shafi'e(الشافعي).

588
00:42:08,554 --> 00:42:11,562
Abu Obaidah(ابو عبيدة) was saying that his words really apply to me,

589
00:42:11,721 --> 00:42:16,194
O Messenger of Allah I've laid my life down for you.

590
00:42:17,226 --> 00:42:18,467
And then he passed away.

591
00:42:18,870 --> 00:42:19,902
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

592
00:42:19,967 --> 00:42:21,511
اَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ شَهِيْدْ

593
00:42:22,357 --> 00:42:24,985
I testify that you are a Shaheed(شهيد).

594
00:42:26,068 --> 00:42:29,892
The Ayaat(آيات) from Surat-Ul-Hajj(سورةالحج) that were revealed about the dueling,

595
00:42:30,065 --> 00:42:31,261
 Allahعَزّوجَلّ says,

596
00:42:31,573 --> 00:42:36,172
هَٰذَانِ خَصْمَانِ اخْتَصَمُوا فِي رَبِّهِمْۖ

597
00:42:36,554 --> 00:42:47,791
فَالَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا قُطِّعَتْ لَهُمْ ثِيَابٌ مِنْنَارٍ يُصَبُّ مِنْ فَوْقِ رُءُوسِهِمُ الْحَمِيمُ۝

598
00:42:48,311 --> 00:42:54,044
يُصْهَرُ بِهِ مَا فِي بُطُونِهِمْ وَالْجُلُودُ۝

599
00:42:54,295 --> 00:42:58,830
وَلَهُمْ مَقَامِعُ مِنْ حَدِيدٍ۝

600
00:42:59,206 --> 00:43:10,959
 كُلَّمَا أَرَادُوا أَنْ يَخْرُجُوا مِنْهَا مِنْ غَمٍّ أُعِيدُوا فِيهَا

601
00:43:11,407 --> 00:43:16,665
أُعِيدُوا فِيهَا وَذُوقُوا عَذَابَ الْحَرِيقِ۝

602
00:43:17,141 --> 00:43:25,950
انَّ اللَّهَ يُدْخِلُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ جَنَّاتٍ

603
00:43:26,606 --> 00:43:38,691
جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهَارُ يُحَلَّوْنَ فِيهَامِنْ أَسَاوِرَ مِنْ ذَهَبٍ وَلُؤْلُؤًا ۖ

604
00:43:39,075 --> 00:43:42,741
وَلِبَاسُهُمْ فِيهَا حَرِيرٌ۝

605
00:43:43,602 --> 00:43:52,657
وَهُدُوا إِلَى الطَّيِّبِ مِنَ الْقَوْلِ وَهُدُوا إِلَىٰ صِرَاطِ الْحَمِيدِ۝

606
00:43:52,887 --> 00:43:55,324
These are two adversaries,

607
00:43:55,851 --> 00:43:58,011
who have disputed over their Lord.

608
00:43:59,107 --> 00:44:03,927
But those who disbelieved will have cut out for them, garments of fire

609
00:44:04,568 --> 00:44:07,797
poured upon their heads will be scalding water

610
00:44:08,987 --> 00:44:12,531
by which is melted that within their bellies and their skins

611
00:44:14,142 --> 00:44:16,603
and for striking them are masses of iron.

612
00:44:18,031 --> 00:44:23,307
Every time they want to get out of it, from anguish, they will be returned to it.

613
00:44:23,921 --> 00:44:28,108
And it will be said, take the punishment of the burning fire.

614
00:44:29,207 --> 00:44:32,165
Indeed, Allah will admit those who believe

615
00:44:32,788 --> 00:44:37,006
and do righteous deeds to gardens beneath which rivers flow.

616
00:44:37,558 --> 00:44:41,677
They will be adorn therein, with bracelets of gold and Pearl

617
00:44:42,022 --> 00:44:44,425
and their garments therein will be silk.

618
00:44:44,837 --> 00:44:48,409
And they had been guided in worldly life to good speech

619
00:44:48,859 --> 00:44:52,314
and they were guided to the path of the Praiseworthy.

620
00:44:53,415 --> 00:44:58,762
Again these Ayaat(آيات) revealed talking about the single combat

621
00:45:00,143 --> 00:45:06,891
Allah-o-Akbar(الله اكبر), the three Muslims defeated the three Mushrikeen(مشركين) in single combat.

622
00:45:07,486 --> 00:45:12,036
And that is when, the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were enraged

623
00:45:12,943 --> 00:45:17,137
and they started advancing towards the Muslims.

624
00:45:18,137 --> 00:45:20,523
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ gave his army instructions,

625
00:45:21,361 --> 00:45:24,486
If they close in, on you then shoot at them,

626
00:45:24,806 --> 00:45:30,625
don't just start firing your arrows haphazardly in a confused state.

627
00:45:31,304 --> 00:45:33,584
 Stay calm, control yourself

628
00:45:34,064 --> 00:45:37,183
and when they close in, on you then start shooting them

629
00:45:37,223 --> 00:45:41,157
and then he said and preserve your arrows, and in another narration, gather them.

630
00:45:41,844 --> 00:45:43,786
See, because they were low in ammo.

631
00:45:44,316 --> 00:45:51,373
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was telling them, preserve your arrows, don't just fire in every direction in a terrified state.

632
00:45:51,632 --> 00:45:55,239
 Wait until, they come close and then start shooting them.

633
00:45:55,479 --> 00:45:56,970
This narration is in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

634
00:45:57,706 --> 00:46:00,235
In another narration in Abu Dawood(أبو داؤد), Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

635
00:46:00,448 --> 00:46:04,095
and do not draw out your swords until, they are near to you.

636
00:46:04,446 --> 00:46:09,423
So, continue firing arrows, and then when it's almost hand to hand combat,

637
00:46:09,661 --> 00:46:11,760
that is when you draw out your swords.

638
00:46:13,421 --> 00:46:15,096
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), when the battle started

639
00:46:16,440 --> 00:46:20,682
the Mushrikeen(مشركين) started seeing the Muslims as double their number.

640
00:46:21,558 --> 00:46:22,998
You remember, we said that

641
00:46:23,381 --> 00:46:28,408
before battle started the Mushrikeen(مشركين) would see the Muslims, as being less than they really are.

642
00:46:28,448 --> 00:46:30,367
 So, they were seeing them as less than 300.

643
00:46:30,834 --> 00:46:32,082
Now when battle started,

644
00:46:32,122 --> 00:46:37,452
suddenly the numbers changed the perception of the size of the Muslim army, changes.

645
00:46:37,845 --> 00:46:45,005
So, the Mushrikeen(مشركين), who are 1000 see the Muslims as being 2000, when they were only 317 or 319.

646
00:46:45,607 --> 00:46:47,131
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says in Qur'an,

647
00:46:47,586 --> 00:46:53,354
قَدْ كَانَ لَكُمْ آيَةٌ فِي فِئَتَيْنِ الْتَقَتَاۖ

648
00:46:53,560 --> 00:47:04,347
 فِئَةٌ تُقَاتِلُ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ وَأُخْرَىٰ كَافِرَةٌ يَرَوْنَهُمْ مِثْلَيْهِمْ رَأْيَ الْعَيْنِۚ

649
00:47:04,747 --> 00:47:10,299
 وَاللَّهُ يُؤَيِّدُ بِنَصْرِهِ مَنْ يَشَاءُ

650
00:47:10,598 --> 00:47:16,831
إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَعِبْرَةً لِأُولِي الْأَبْصَارِ۝

651
00:47:17,731 --> 00:47:21,655
Already there has been for you a sign in the two armies which met,

652
00:47:22,161 --> 00:47:26,513
one fighting in the cause of Allah, and another of disbelievers.

653
00:47:27,477 --> 00:47:31,662
They saw them to be twice their own number by their eyesight.

654
00:47:32,140 --> 00:47:35,279
But Allah supports with His victory, whom He wills.

655
00:47:35,720 --> 00:47:39,728
Indeed, in that is a lesson for those of vision.

656
00:47:40,466 --> 00:47:43,711
So, in the beginning, they see them as less than their own number,

657
00:47:43,892 --> 00:47:47,468
so that they would be careless and they would be willing to fight.

658
00:47:48,409 --> 00:47:50,596
However, when fighting does actually start,

659
00:47:50,928 --> 00:47:55,058
they will see them as double their numbers, so that this will destroy their morale.

660
00:47:56,164 --> 00:48:01,023
And the Muslims had the battle cry, a war cry

661
00:48:01,258 --> 00:48:03,923
and that was Ahad(أحد), Ahad(أحد), Ahad(أحد), Ahad(أحد),

662
00:48:04,067 --> 00:48:07,989
One, One, One, One that was their war cry.

663
00:48:09,269 --> 00:48:12,664
And this was something that the Muslims would employ in their battles,

664
00:48:12,721 --> 00:48:17,387
 they would have a certain a fixed war cry that they would keep on repeating.

665
00:48:19,171 --> 00:48:24,109
Harissa رضي الله عنه, one of the Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار) was shot by a stray arrow,

666
00:48:24,618 --> 00:48:26,919
so he was killed by friendly fire.

667
00:48:27,812 --> 00:48:31,125
When The battle was over, and his mother met with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

668
00:48:31,170 --> 00:48:31,927
She said;

669
00:48:32,178 --> 00:48:37,718
Tell me whether Harissa(حارثه) is in Paradise, so that I'll be happy

670
00:48:37,798 --> 00:48:40,004
or if he's not, then I'll cry for him.

671
00:48:40,562 --> 00:48:43,599
Rasool told her; Have you gone crazy.

672
00:48:44,183 --> 00:48:46,793
There are plenty ofgardens in Paradise,

673
00:48:47,156 --> 00:48:49,944
and your son has earned the very highest of them.

674
00:48:51,442 --> 00:48:54,240
Your son is in the highest level of Jannah(جنة).

675
00:48:54,954 --> 00:49:01,447
Because Allahعَزّوجَلّ has prepared exclusively for the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) One Hundred levels on top of Al-Jannah(جنة)

676
00:49:01,921 --> 00:49:03,988
and Harissa(حارثه) is in the highest one.

677
00:49:06,620 --> 00:49:07,648
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

678
00:49:08,544 --> 00:49:14,576
وَلَقَدْ نَصَرَكُمُ اللَّهُ بِبَدْرٍ وَأَنْتُمْ أَذِلَّةٌ

679
00:49:14,902 --> 00:49:19,060
فَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُونَ۝

680
00:49:19,430 --> 00:49:29,415
إِذْ تَقُولُ لِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ أَلَنْ يَكْفِيَكُمْ أَنْ يُمِدَّكُمْ رَبُّكُمْ بِثَلَاثَةِ آلَافٍ

681
00:49:29,821 --> 00:49:36,618
بِثَلَاثَةِ آلَافٍ مِنَ الْمَلَائِكَةِ مُنْزَلِينَ۝

682
00:49:37,030 --> 00:49:38,066
بَلَىٰ

683
00:49:38,340 --> 00:49:45,313
إِنْ تَصْبِرُوا وَتَتَّقُوا وَيَأْتُوكُمْ مِنْ فَوْرِهِمْ هَٰذَا

684
00:49:45,573 --> 00:49:55,398
هَٰذَا يُمْدِدْكُمْ رَبُّكُمْ بِخَمْسَةِ آلَافٍ مِنَ الْمَلَائِكَةِ مُسَوِّمِينَ۝

685
00:49:55,846 --> 00:50:03,824
 وَمَا جَعَلَهُ اللَّهُ إِلَّا بُشْرَىٰ لَكُمْ وَلِتَطْمَئِنَّ قُلُوبُكُمْ بِهِ

686
00:50:04,034 --> 00:50:11,509
وَمَا النَّصْرُ إِلَّا مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ الْعَزِيزِ الْحَكِيمِ۝

687
00:50:12,215 --> 00:50:18,496
And already had Allah given you victory at the Battle of Badr(بدر), while you were weak,

688
00:50:19,134 --> 00:50:23,235
meaning few in number, then fear Allah perhaps you will be grateful.

689
00:50:24,016 --> 00:50:26,241
Remember when you said to the believers

690
00:50:26,728 --> 00:50:33,462
is it not sufficient for you that your Lord should reinforce you with 3000 Angels sent down,

691
00:50:33,854 --> 00:50:35,980
previously We said, it was thousand.

692
00:50:36,530 --> 00:50:39,831
So, that was the minimum number Allahعَزّوجَلّ could have sent to them.

693
00:50:40,422 --> 00:50:44,174
But then the number could be 3000 or it could be more like 5000.

694
00:50:44,474 --> 00:50:45,891
And then Allah says; Yes

695
00:50:46,310 --> 00:50:49,157
If you remain patient and conscious of Allah

696
00:50:49,360 --> 00:50:52,757
and they, the enemy come upon you attacking in rage

697
00:50:53,029 --> 00:50:58,612
your Lord will reinforce you with 5000 angels having marks of distinction

698
00:50:59,511 --> 00:51:03,380
and Allah made it not accept as a sign of good tidings for you

699
00:51:03,860 --> 00:51:06,250
and to reassure your hearts thereby.

700
00:51:06,650 --> 00:51:10,103
And victory is not accept from Allah, meaning you don't really need the Angels.

701
00:51:10,701 --> 00:51:15,330
This was a sign of good tidings for you and to reassure your hearts

702
00:51:15,696 --> 00:51:19,682
and victory is not except from Allah, the Exalted in Might, the Wise.

703
00:51:20,423 --> 00:51:23,997
So, in what form did the Angels participate in this battle.

704
00:51:25,695 --> 00:51:27,766
Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) himself joined in

705
00:51:28,468 --> 00:51:34,066
Rasool Allah ﷺ says; I saw Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) taking his horse by the reins and leading it.

706
00:51:35,100 --> 00:51:37,650
And all of the angels were wearing white turbans,

707
00:51:37,690 --> 00:51:41,135
except Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل), he was wearing a yellow one to distinguish him.

708
00:51:41,394 --> 00:51:45,872
 He was the leader of the army of angels on that day.

709
00:51:47,262 --> 00:51:48,362
In Sahih Muslim(صحيح مسلم),

710
00:51:48,701 --> 00:51:54,681
it says while one of the Muslim warriors was vigorously pursuing one of the unbelievers ahead of him,

711
00:51:54,988 --> 00:51:58,223
He heard above him the noise of a whip striking

712
00:51:58,490 --> 00:52:00,121
and a rider's voice saying:

713
00:52:00,193 --> 00:52:02,552
 غِدِّيْ اَبْ هَيْزُوْمْ ، اَقْدِمْ هَيْزُوْمْ

714
00:52:03,561 --> 00:52:07,516
When the Muslim warrior looked at the Polytheist in front of him,

715
00:52:07,833 --> 00:52:09,991
he found him prostrate on the ground.

716
00:52:10,471 --> 00:52:15,671
Examining him more closely, he found that the man's nose has been smashed

717
00:52:15,920 --> 00:52:21,141
and his face split apart by a blow from a whip, all having turned black in color.

718
00:52:21,322 --> 00:52:22,738
 So, this was a whip of fire.

719
00:52:23,775 --> 00:52:28,042
The warrior, An Ansaari(انصاري), went and told this, to the Messenger of Allah, Who said;

720
00:52:28,100 --> 00:52:31,895
You speak true that was help from the third heaven.

721
00:52:32,277 --> 00:52:35,654
 So, this was an angel riding on a horse called Hayzoom(هيزوم)

722
00:52:36,024 --> 00:52:36,657
And he was saying:

723
00:52:36,697 --> 00:52:39,261
 غِدِّيْ اَبْ هَيْزُوْمْ ، اَقْدِمْ، اَقْدِمْ هَيْزُوْمْ

724
00:52:40,003 --> 00:52:42,717
Ibn Is'haqq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ) narrates another story, he said;

725
00:52:43,549 --> 00:52:50,691
A Ghafari(غفاري) man said, I and a cousin of mine, were present at Badr(بدر), though we were still Polytheist, then.

726
00:52:50,762 --> 00:52:53,988
 So, these were two young men who were Mushrikeen(مشركين),

727
00:52:54,458 --> 00:52:57,638
and they were there just to watch the battle

728
00:52:57,948 --> 00:52:59,335
they wanted to see who would win,

729
00:52:59,375 --> 00:53:02,404
they had no quarrel with either side, they had nothing to do with the battle

730
00:53:02,605 --> 00:53:04,641
they just went there as spectators.

731
00:53:05,505 --> 00:53:09,943
We were up on a mountain waiting for the battle to take place and to see, who would win.

732
00:53:10,267 --> 00:53:11,797
When a cloud approached.

733
00:53:12,252 --> 00:53:18,234
When it drew near the mountain we heard the sound of horses galloping, and a voice saying;

734
00:53:18,314 --> 00:53:21,243
 اَقْدِمْ هَيْزُوْمْ ،غِدِّيْ اَبْ هَيْزُوْمْ ،

735
00:53:21,918 --> 00:53:24,915
My companion suffered a heart attack and died on the spot,

736
00:53:25,700 --> 00:53:28,404
while I almost expired, but later recovered.

737
00:53:28,467 --> 00:53:32,952
So, this was quite a shock for these two men, one of them had a heart attack.

738
00:53:34,725 --> 00:53:36,089
Al-Mazini(ألمازني) says;

739
00:53:36,383 --> 00:53:42,621
that while I was pursuing one of the Mushrikeen(مشركين), in front of me suddenly in his head flew off.

740
00:53:42,877 --> 00:53:46,295
So I realized that he was killed by someone other than me.

741
00:53:47,414 --> 00:53:58,250
And they could distinguish the casualties, caused by the angels compared to those caused by the believers.

742
00:53:58,462 --> 00:53:59,845
Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) said;

743
00:54:00,107 --> 00:54:06,570
Our men could differentiate the ones, the angels had killed from those, they had struck by the blow

744
00:54:07,311 --> 00:54:14,680
having occurred above their necks and by their fingertips looking as if they had been burned by a branding iron.

745
00:54:15,021 --> 00:54:19,599
So, the deaths that were caused by the angels, you can know that these were caused by the angels,

746
00:54:19,837 --> 00:54:21,734
first of all, because it was a clean cut

747
00:54:22,011 --> 00:54:30,226
and then because it was black, it was burned, as if it was a branding iron, that was striking them.

748
00:54:31,061 --> 00:54:36,384
Not only did the angels kill but they also captured prisoners of war.

749
00:54:36,424 --> 00:54:37,571
 Al-Abbas(العباس) says;

750
00:54:37,792 --> 00:54:44,499
Ya'ani(يعني) when one of Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار) was dragging Al-Abbas(العباس) and he's saying that he captured him.

751
00:54:44,734 --> 00:54:49,083
Al-Abbas(العباس) said; O Messenger ofAllah, this is not the man, who captured me.

752
00:54:49,415 --> 00:54:52,940
A bald, fine looking man on a pie bald horse,

753
00:54:53,321 --> 00:54:57,336
whom I had not seen with your men, was he, who took me prisoner.

754
00:54:57,844 --> 00:55:01,568
So, The Ansaari(أنصاري) said: No, It was I, who captured him, O Messenger of Allah.

755
00:55:01,935 --> 00:55:06,905
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Keep quiet! Allah gave you help of a noble Angel.

756
00:55:08,398 --> 00:55:10,480
Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهsaid;

757
00:55:10,723 --> 00:55:14,862
the only battle in which the angels participated was at Badr(بدر)

758
00:55:15,187 --> 00:55:22,127
at the other battles, they constituted auxiliaries and reinforcements, that did not actually fight.

759
00:55:23,569 --> 00:55:27,404
The death toll seventy Mushrikeen(مشركين), were killed

760
00:55:27,822 --> 00:55:30,166
and 70 were taken prisoners of war.

761
00:55:30,389 --> 00:55:33,805
Among the Muslims, no prisoners of war whatsoever.

762
00:55:34,083 --> 00:55:35,763
And there were 14 deaths,

763
00:55:36,354 --> 00:55:38,717
Six from among Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون),

764
00:55:39,098 --> 00:55:41,066
six from among Al-Khazraj(ألخزرج),

765
00:55:41,304 --> 00:55:43,336
and two from among Al-Aos(ألأوس).

766
00:55:44,551 --> 00:55:47,021
Some scenes from the battlefield.

767
00:55:47,831 --> 00:55:51,529
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf رضي الله عنه, said;

768
00:55:51,569 --> 00:55:58,128
he was flanked by two young men in the rank in the line, in the battle.

769
00:55:58,792 --> 00:56:01,421
He was flanked by two youngmen.

770
00:56:02,223 --> 00:56:07,332
Now, soldiers, know, you want to have good soldiers on your right and on your left.

771
00:56:08,673 --> 00:56:12,835
You want to have good fighting companions, by your side.

772
00:56:14,059 --> 00:56:18,891
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) wasn't happy that he has these two kids next to him.

773
00:56:19,613 --> 00:56:21,527
Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) was a mature man.

774
00:56:21,908 --> 00:56:24,178
And he had these young men next to him.

775
00:56:24,218 --> 00:56:28,456
So he preferred to have someone else flanking him.

776
00:56:29,829 --> 00:56:33,753
And then he said the one to my right.

777
00:56:34,468 --> 00:56:39,966
He whispered to me and said; O uncle show me which one is Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل).

778
00:56:40,581 --> 00:56:44,139
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) said; O, my son, What do you want with Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل).

779
00:56:44,987 --> 00:56:46,306
This young man said;

780
00:56:46,774 --> 00:56:53,004
I swore to Allah, that if I saw him, I would kill him or die in front of him.

781
00:56:53,432 --> 00:56:55,901
Either I kill him or I die right there.

782
00:56:57,389 --> 00:57:03,278
So, now Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمنإبن عوف) is starting to change his mind about who's flanking him.

783
00:57:03,715 --> 00:57:07,070
 You know, Don't base your opinion based on the looks.

784
00:57:07,707 --> 00:57:10,388
Don't make a judgment based on the looks.

785
00:57:11,442 --> 00:57:18,358
This man right next to you wants to kill Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل), the leader of the army of Al-Mushrikeen(المشركين).

786
00:57:19,715 --> 00:57:23,980
And then he points out Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) to this young man to his right.

787
00:57:24,518 --> 00:57:26,058
Now the young man to his left

788
00:57:26,137 --> 00:57:29,617
whispers in the ear of Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) and asked him the same question.

789
00:57:30,527 --> 00:57:32,241
And the reason why, they're whispering is.?

790
00:57:32,557 --> 00:57:36,099
These two brothers were competing with each other.

791
00:57:36,139 --> 00:57:40,257
So they were whispering to Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف), so that other one doesn't hear.

792
00:57:41,691 --> 00:57:43,352
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) said;

793
00:57:43,487 --> 00:57:47,566
When I showed Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) to them, and he pointed out and he said;

794
00:57:48,367 --> 00:57:49,550
See that man,

795
00:57:49,852 --> 00:57:54,447
you know, it was like a crowd around Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل), all of them protecting him,

796
00:57:54,518 --> 00:57:56,972
so he pointed out Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) and said that's Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل).

797
00:57:57,814 --> 00:58:01,734
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) said, they flew at him like Falcons.

798
00:58:02,406 --> 00:58:08,275
This was in Al-Bukhari(البخاريْ), they flew at him as Falcons, and they struck him down.

799
00:58:09,378 --> 00:58:14,143
They struck Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) down, two young men, from among Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار).

800
00:58:15,326 --> 00:58:18,227
These two young men, according to one narration are

801
00:58:18,620 --> 00:58:21,011
Muadh Ibn Amr BinJamooh(معاذ إبن عمرو بن الجموح)

802
00:58:21,476 --> 00:58:24,350
and Muawwiz(معوذ) or Auf Bin Afraah(عوف بن أفراح).

803
00:58:24,627 --> 00:58:25,659
And in another narration,

804
00:58:25,762 --> 00:58:32,502
they are two brothers, Auf(عوف) and Muawwiz Bin Ibn Al-Hariss(معوذ بن حارث), whose mother was Afrah(أفراح).

805
00:58:33,127 --> 00:58:40,000
In another narration, it says that when they attacked Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل), and they reached next to him.

806
00:58:40,412 --> 00:58:43,843
One of them struck the foot of Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل).

807
00:58:44,010 --> 00:58:49,400
So, it flew off like a kernel of nut would fly off from the Nut cracker.

808
00:58:50,178 --> 00:58:54,218
 And it made that sound of a crack and then it flew off.

809
00:58:54,932 --> 00:59:03,771
 But then Ikrimah(إكرمه) saw that and he struck Muadh(معاذ) on his shoulder and he tore off his arm.

810
00:59:04,252 --> 00:59:12,683
However, the arm remained, hanging to his body by the flesh of his side, of his chest.

811
00:59:13,726 --> 00:59:20,630
So, the joint itself is tore away, is cut, but the arm is still is just dangling by his side.

812
00:59:21,221 --> 00:59:25,439
And Muadh(معاذ) said: I carried on fighting, dragging my arm behind me,

813
00:59:26,065 --> 00:59:29,541
until it started bothering me and distracting me from fighting,

814
00:59:30,148 --> 00:59:34,223
so I placed it under my foot and stepped over it and tore it off.

815
00:59:35,167 --> 00:59:36,721
That's quite a thing to do.

816
00:59:37,435 --> 00:59:44,991
So, Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) was killed, or was disabled by these two young Ansaari(أنصاري) men.

817
00:59:45,546 --> 00:59:50,824
But he was laying there on the ground on the battlefield, in his last moments.

818
00:59:51,980 --> 00:59:54,761
Rasool Allah ﷺ, asked the Sahabah and said;

819
00:59:55,018 --> 00:59:57,958
who would find out for me, What happened to Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل).

820
00:59:58,589 --> 01:00:00,465
Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) said: so I went,

821
01:00:01,466 --> 01:00:07,394
and when I realize that the man laying in front of me, was Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل).

822
01:00:08,378 --> 01:00:11,309
I stepped over his neck with my foot.

823
01:00:11,958 --> 01:00:15,303
He said when I recognized him, I put my foot on his neck.

824
01:00:15,886 --> 01:00:20,732
He had once held me captive in Makkah and hurt me and kicked me.

825
01:00:21,107 --> 01:00:25,595
And then he asked him, he said, so Allah has put you to shame then, you enemy of Allah.

826
01:00:26,169 --> 01:00:27,420
Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) is saying

827
01:00:27,492 --> 01:00:29,999
that Allah has shamed you, you enemyof Allah.

828
01:00:30,039 --> 01:00:31,681
Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) said;

829
01:00:32,106 --> 01:00:34,118
And how has, He shamed me

830
01:00:34,542 --> 01:00:38,529
Aren't I the most noble man you have ever killed.

831
01:00:39,116 --> 01:00:41,823
Tell me which side won the day?

832
01:00:42,414 --> 01:00:47,917
Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) even though he's in his last moments wants to know the result of this battle.

833
01:00:48,560 --> 01:00:52,445
Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) said; it went to Allah and His messenger.

834
01:00:53,616 --> 01:00:56,157
In another narration, It says that

835
01:00:56,291 --> 01:00:57,624
Abdullah Bin Masood(عبداللهبن مسعود) is saying that

836
01:00:57,698 --> 01:01:04,104
Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) was laying on the ground, holding a fine sword and protecting himself,

837
01:01:04,659 --> 01:01:06,480
 while I had the poor sword.

838
01:01:06,876 --> 01:01:12,580
So, I struck his arm so his sword fell off and then I carried his sword.

839
01:01:13,048 --> 01:01:18,342
And I sat on his chest to sever his head, and when I was over his chest.

840
01:01:18,382 --> 01:01:19,302
He said;

841
01:01:19,441 --> 01:01:22,843
لَقَدْاِرْتَقَيْتَ مُرْتَقًا صعْبًا يَا رُوَيعِيَّ الْغَنَمْ

842
01:01:23,614 --> 01:01:28,166
You've climbed very high for having being just a herdsman.

843
01:01:28,660 --> 01:01:31,834
Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) is arrogant even when he's dying.

844
01:01:32,628 --> 01:01:34,822
He's telling Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) that

845
01:01:35,248 --> 01:01:40,166
for you to be on top of my chest is too high of a place for you.

846
01:01:40,771 --> 01:01:45,278
Because you are but, a herdsmen, you are a Raee(راعي), Ra'al Ghanam(راعي  الغنم).

847
01:01:45,864 --> 01:01:48,349
Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) said: I then severed his head

848
01:01:48,948 --> 01:01:51,968
and took it to the messengerof Allah ﷺ.

849
01:01:52,813 --> 01:01:53,802
Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) said;

850
01:01:53,842 --> 01:01:56,175
I was as though walking on air,

851
01:01:56,219 --> 01:02:06,237
he was flying in the air, speeding off, Happy, to go and deliver the head of Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

852
01:02:06,879 --> 01:02:12,319
I said: this, O Messenger of Allah is the head of Allah's enemy.

853
01:02:12,708 --> 01:02:14,305
 Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

854
01:02:14,811 --> 01:02:17,861
Is it really, By Allah other than whom there is none.

855
01:02:18,138 --> 01:02:19,138
I said: Yes

856
01:02:19,507 --> 01:02:24,264
And then I threw Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل)'s head down in front of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

857
01:02:24,525 --> 01:02:26,176
who then praised Allah(عَزّوجَلّ).

858
01:02:26,255 --> 01:02:28,890
 In the narration of Imam Ahmad, Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

859
01:02:28,972 --> 01:02:33,890
Al-Hamdolillah(ألحمدلله) Allah has disgraced you, your enemy of Allah.

860
01:02:34,123 --> 01:02:36,803
This man was the Pharaoh of his people.

861
01:02:37,540 --> 01:02:39,525
Every nation has a Firoun(فرعون)

862
01:02:39,882 --> 01:02:43,126
and the Firoun(فرعون) of our nation is Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل).

863
01:02:44,049 --> 01:02:46,855
Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) comments on the death of Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) and he said;

864
01:02:47,293 --> 01:02:51,673
the death of Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) came about at the hands of a youth from Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار)

865
01:02:52,507 --> 01:02:55,761
their after Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) was placed over him.

866
01:02:56,255 --> 01:02:59,642
So, look at who Allah chose to kill Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل),

867
01:03:00,287 --> 01:03:02,857
two young men from Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار) and Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود).

868
01:03:02,882 --> 01:03:05,539
Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود), who was belittled by Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل)

869
01:03:05,879 --> 01:03:08,340
Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود), who was very slightly built.

870
01:03:08,396 --> 01:03:09,467
He was very thin.

871
01:03:09,847 --> 01:03:17,263
One day he was climbing a palm tree and there was wind blowing, and it shook Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود),

872
01:03:18,017 --> 01:03:19,240
 he was very light weight.

873
01:03:19,820 --> 01:03:25,393
And the Sahabah laughed when they saw the thinness of the legs of Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود).

874
01:03:25,671 --> 01:03:27,324
 So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said

875
01:03:27,704 --> 01:03:29,586
اَتَضْحَكُوْنَ لِدِقَّة سَاقيه

876
01:03:29,931 --> 01:03:33,093
Are you laughing because he has very slim legs

877
01:03:33,556 --> 01:03:39,175
In the name of Allah, they are heavier on the scale on the Day of Judgment than the mountain of Uhud(احد).

878
01:03:39,795 --> 01:03:43,112
It's not by how pounds you can carry

879
01:03:43,379 --> 01:03:46,079
and how well built you are

880
01:03:46,414 --> 01:03:50,240
and how athletic you are and how powerful and strong you are.

881
01:03:50,722 --> 01:03:56,089
Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل), the leaderof the enemy's army was killed by Abdullah Bin Masood رضي الله عنه

882
01:03:56,321 --> 01:03:58,367
and by two young men from Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار).

883
01:03:59,737 --> 01:04:02,693
We shouldn't depend on worldly standards.

884
01:04:03,716 --> 01:04:08,418
How strong the soldier is how muscular he is.

885
01:04:08,830 --> 01:04:15,653
A Muslim soldier is supposed to prepare, but not to depend on that preparation, you depend on Allah.

886
01:04:16,752 --> 01:04:17,788
So, Ibn Kathir(إبن كثير) said;

887
01:04:18,265 --> 01:04:22,348
the death of Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) came about at the hands of a youth from Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار).

888
01:04:22,738 --> 01:04:25,574
Their after Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) was placed over him,

889
01:04:26,136 --> 01:04:28,804
by this Allah comforted the believers.

890
01:04:29,122 --> 01:04:34,667
And this was more effective than if He had made a bolt of lightning strike Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) down

891
01:04:35,089 --> 01:04:37,353
or made the roof of his house fall upon him

892
01:04:37,707 --> 01:04:39,996
or if he had died a natural death.

893
01:04:40,290 --> 01:04:42,377
And then he recited the Ayah(آية) of Allah

894
01:04:42,944 --> 01:04:56,156
قَاتِلُوهُمْ يُعَذِّبْهُمُ اللَّهُ بِأَيْدِيكُمْ وَيُخْزِهِمْوَيَنْصُرْكُمْ عَلَيْهِمْ وَيَشْفِ صُدُورَ قَوْمٍ مُؤْمِنِينَ۝

895
01:04:56,786 --> 01:05:08,559
وَيُذْهِبْ غَيْظَ قُلُوبِهِمْ ۗ وَيَتُوبُ اللَّهُعَلَىٰ مَنْ يَشَاءُ ۗ وَاللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ حَكِيمٌ۝

896
01:05:08,901 --> 01:05:12,226
Fight them, Allah will punish them by your hands,

897
01:05:12,474 --> 01:05:14,274
not by lightning.

898
01:05:14,599 --> 01:05:17,925
As Ibn Kathir(إبن كثير) says; Dying a natural death.

899
01:05:18,194 --> 01:05:20,226
 Allah will punish them, by your hands

900
01:05:20,889 --> 01:05:24,337
and will disgrace them and give you victory over them

901
01:05:24,676 --> 01:05:27,677
and satisfy the breasts of a believing people,

902
01:05:28,106 --> 01:05:30,653
and remove the fury in their hearts

903
01:05:31,074 --> 01:05:35,728
and Allah turns in forgiveness to whom He wills and Allah is Knowing and Wise.

904
01:05:36,523 --> 01:05:38,410
So, there's an element of revenge here because

905
01:05:38,664 --> 01:05:41,109
Muslims have been wronged, they've been oppressed

906
01:05:41,522 --> 01:05:44,720
So, Allah is saying that he will satisfy your breasts

907
01:05:45,336 --> 01:05:47,216
and remove the fury in your hearts.

908
01:05:47,271 --> 01:05:49,619
The Muslims were furious at the Kuffar(كفار)

909
01:05:49,982 --> 01:05:54,114
so Allah will remove that, when they see the faith of the enemies of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

910
01:05:55,528 --> 01:05:59,096
One of the famous fighters of Al-Mushrikeen(المشركين)

911
01:05:59,976 --> 01:06:04,406
he was nicknamed, Abul Kirsh(ابو الكرش), the one with the potbelly.

912
01:06:05,253 --> 01:06:08,680
He was covered in armor, you could only see his eyes.

913
01:06:09,437 --> 01:06:12,156
So, Az-Zubair Bin Awwamرضي الله عنه attacked him,

914
01:06:13,098 --> 01:06:15,984
but again this is a man covered in steel from head to toe.

915
01:06:16,901 --> 01:06:19,486
Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(الزبير بن عوام), with his javelins

916
01:06:19,511 --> 01:06:24,523
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), he was able to strike him right in that small opening in the eye.

917
01:06:25,400 --> 01:06:30,347
But the opening was so small, so the spear, the javelin cannot go through.

918
01:06:30,744 --> 01:06:35,421
 So, Az-Zubair(الزبير) steps on his Javelin with his foot

919
01:06:35,889 --> 01:06:40,534
 and forces it deep into the head of Abul Kirsh(ابو الكرش).

920
01:06:41,625 --> 01:06:47,094
So, when he pulls out his Javelin, the blade was bent, so bad

921
01:06:47,967 --> 01:06:51,698
and this shows you the strength of Az-Zubair Bin Awwam رضي الله عنه,

922
01:06:52,557 --> 01:06:57,018
it was amazing that the blade was bent in such a fashion.

923
01:06:57,649 --> 01:07:00,755
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ asked to keep that Javelin as a souvenir

924
01:07:01,606 --> 01:07:05,076
And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), when Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away, Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) asked for it.

925
01:07:05,691 --> 01:07:08,132
And when Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) passed away, Umar(عُمَر) asked for it,

926
01:07:08,420 --> 01:07:11,780
and when Umar(عُمَر) pass away, Az-Zubair(الزبير) got it, back again, it was his

927
01:07:12,068 --> 01:07:15,081
but then Uthman(عثمان) asked Az-Zubair(الزبير) to give it to him.

928
01:07:15,690 --> 01:07:18,922
So, Az-Zubair(الزبير) hands it over to the Khalifah(خليفه) Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان).

929
01:07:19,423 --> 01:07:21,899
And when Uthman(عثمان) passes away, Ali(علي) takes it,

930
01:07:22,371 --> 01:07:27,033
and then after Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب), Abdullah Bin Zubair(عبدالله بن زبير), the son of Zubair(الزبير), gets it.

931
01:07:27,980 --> 01:07:31,258
Abul-Bukhtari(ابوا لبختري) was one of the noble man of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

932
01:07:31,321 --> 01:07:36,675
He was a Mushrik(مشرك), a disbeliever but he wasn't cruel against the Muslims.

933
01:07:37,220 --> 01:07:47,141
In fact, he was one of the men, who participated in the ending of the siege, against the Muslims.

934
01:07:47,595 --> 01:07:48,824
If you remember in Makkah,

935
01:07:49,284 --> 01:07:54,149
there was a siege that lasted for three years against Bannu Hashim(بنو هاشم) and Bannu Ul-Muttalib(بنوالمطلب),

936
01:07:54,385 --> 01:07:56,184
the family of Rasool Allahﷺ.

937
01:07:56,962 --> 01:08:02,200
Abul Bukhtari(ابولبختري) was one of the men, who ended this siege.

938
01:08:02,754 --> 01:08:09,799
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was grateful to him and he asked the Muslims not to kill him, if you see him in battle.

939
01:08:10,351 --> 01:08:13,511
So there's a lesson to learn here

940
01:08:13,551 --> 01:08:17,543
you know that some Mushrikeen(مشركين), even though they are Mushrikeen(مشركين), they are disbelievers

941
01:08:18,032 --> 01:08:21,605
 but if they do you good, then reciprocate.

942
01:08:22,220 --> 01:08:24,918
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said, If you see him, Don't kill him, leave him.

943
01:08:25,623 --> 01:08:29,136
 So, one of Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار) saw Al-Bukhtari Bin Hishaam(ألبختري بن هشام) and told him

944
01:08:29,176 --> 01:08:31,425
that Rasool Allahﷺ told us not to kill you.

945
01:08:32,247 --> 01:08:35,162
Al-Bukhtari(البختري) said; What about my companion? He had a friend with him.

946
01:08:35,432 --> 01:08:38,987
He said, Well no, we're not going to spare your companion death.

947
01:08:39,035 --> 01:08:39,956
We're going to kill him.

948
01:08:40,146 --> 01:08:41,479
Al-Bukhtari Bin Hisham(ألبختري بن هشام) said;

949
01:08:41,835 --> 01:08:47,004
then I'm going to protect my companion, I'm going to fight to protect him.

950
01:08:47,603 --> 01:08:53,964
And thus, the Ansari(انصاري) was forced to fight Al-Bukhtari(البختري), and he was killed.

951
01:08:54,282 --> 01:08:57,122
Then he went back to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said,

952
01:08:57,773 --> 01:09:00,127
I swear by Him, Who sent you with the truth,

953
01:09:00,551 --> 01:09:03,554
I did try to take him prisoner to bring him to you,

954
01:09:03,978 --> 01:09:05,741
but he insisted on fighting me.

955
01:09:05,995 --> 01:09:07,932
So, I fought back and killed him.

956
01:09:09,395 --> 01:09:13,118
 رَبَّنَا آتِنَا فِي الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً وَفِي الْآخِرَةِ حَسَنَةً وَقِنَا عَذَابَ النَّارِ۝

957
01:09:13,543 --> 01:09:18,048
وَصَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

958
01:09:18,273 --> 01:09:20,588
وَالسلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

